window.OSAP_FT=window.OSAP_FT||{};window.OSAP_FT["2f"]={"https://theconversation.com/view-from-the-hill-backpacker-compromise-another-example-of-albanese-government-folding-its-cards-296271":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"dc7a5d5eb3a8f4681f6dd8f4ba916a5312abc090301ee5116301e80056f6b1e4","read":"https://theconversation.com/view-from-the-hill-backpacker-compromise-another-example-of-albanese-government-folding-its-cards-296271","bytes":177266,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"View from The Hill: backpacker compromise another example of Albanese government ‘folding its cards’","by":[{"n":"Michelle Grattan","r":"Professorial Fellow, University of Canberra"}],"pub":"2026-11-17T08:13:20Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Home Affairs Minister Tony Burke on Tuesday sought to remove yet another political irritant, when he announced an overhaul of the government’s new rules for working holiday makers."]},{"k":"p","s":["The government was following a course that has many names. John Howard’s chief of staff Arthur Sinodinos famously used to talk about scraping off “barnacles”. The media loves the label “backflips”. Anthony Albanese would no doubt prefer the more benign-sounding “changing our position”."]},{"k":"p","s":["It all amounts to one thing – cutting or limiting losses when a decision becomes a severe political problem. A policy decision is announced, there’s a backlash from vested interests and or the wider community. The government hangs tough for a while, then it gives in and modifies or abandons its original plan. Sometimes trouble in the Senate is in the mix. Sometimes change follows consultations."]},{"k":"p","s":["Politically, the trick is, in the words of ",["The Gambler","https://youtu.be/7hx4gdlfamo"],","]},{"k":"p","s":["You’ve got to know when to hold ‘em"]},{"k":"p","s":["Know when to fold 'em"]},{"k":"p","s":["Know when to walk away"]},{"k":"p","s":["And know when to run."]},{"k":"p","s":["On backpackers, Burke is stepping away from details of his original version while insisting the regions will be better off under his revamp, but the Net Overseas Migration (NOM) won’t be affected."]},{"k":"p","s":["Under his latest model, the number of first year backpackers has been slowed, but the number allowed a third year is increased, while the number of hours worked in the regions will be boosted overall. The ballot announced originally has been modified and renamed an “invitation”."]},{"k":"p","s":["The opposition sees a con. Time will tell whether the policy works, in terms of labour force and the politics."]},{"k":"p","s":["The point is, the government came under pressure from stakeholders and the present mood is to respond where possible, rather than let unpopular decisions fester."]},{"k":"p","s":["It was the same on a very different front: the sell-off of surplus defence properties. There was a hoo-ha about the planned sale of the historic Victoria Barracks in Sydney, with Defence Minister Richard Marles misjudging the mood when he said, “It’s not my priority to see Defence manage the oldest wine cellar in Australia. It’s nice that it’s at Victoria Barracks Sydney, but it’s not core interest in terms of defending the country.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["After a campaign against the sale, the government declared Victoria Barracks and some other high-profile properties were to be taken off the list."]},{"k":"p","s":["Earlier, after a big campaign from critics, the government retreated from a proposed $5,000 cap on support for allied health services for veterans."]},{"k":"p","s":["The budget tax changes have seen plenty of concessions made."]},{"k":"p","s":["When the Australian Taxation Office announced it would ban the use of credit cards to pay tax bills, the government backed it briefly, then stepped in to cover the cost of delaying the measure until mid next year while there were further consultations. You can bet there will be some workaround at the least."]},{"k":"p","s":["In October, the government retreated from a plan to split disaster recover funding with the states on a 50-50 basis, which would have left them worse off."]},{"k":"p","s":["The big outstanding decision with a question mark over its durability is the budget measure that will cut the extra rebate older Australians get on their private health insurance cover. The Greens say they will only pass it if pensioners are excluded. The saving is put at $3 billion over the budget period; a carve out of pensioners would take $1.6 billion."]},{"k":"p","s":["The government has to decide whether to try to stare down the Greens, at the risk of forfeiting all the savings, or get what it can by compromising."]},{"k":"p","s":["Many backtracks cost the budget a greater or lesser amount. In the case of the health insurance rebate, there would be a cost in retreating – and an even bigger one, if the Greens held out, in not retreating."]},{"k":"p","s":["As the words of the song go,"]},{"k":"p","s":["Every gambler knows"]},{"k":"p","s":["That the secret to survivin’"]},{"k":"p","s":["Is knowin’ what to throw away"]},{"k":"p","s":["And knowin’ what to keep."]}],"chars":3858},"https://theconversation.com/myanmars-el-nino-threat-shows-why-extreme-heat-is-also-a-question-of-inequality-294870":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"6aa9b17e88606bb1c85b3a8a642d6a26782f343c6310006cc66f10b1f5939d7b","read":"https://theconversation.com/myanmars-el-nino-threat-shows-why-extreme-heat-is-also-a-question-of-inequality-294870","bytes":180778,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Myanmar’s El Niño threat shows why extreme heat is also a question of inequality","by":[{"n":"Hein Thu","r":"PhD candidate, National University of Singapore"},{"n":"Shahmir Hassan Ali","r":"Assistant Professor of Public Health, National University of Singapore"}],"pub":"2026-11-10T03:11:26Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["A historically strong El Niño is underway. US forecasters expect ",["a strong to very strong event to continue into early 2027","https://www.cpc.ncep.noaa.gov/products/analysis_monitoring/enso_advisory/ensodisc.shtml"],". In Myanmar, ",["meteorologists","https://www.gnlm.com.mm/prepare-early-to-meet-super-el-ninos-challenges/"]," warn that its effects could extend into the hot season from March to May."]},{"k":"p","s":["Forecasts can estimate how high temperatures will rise. But they cannot predict who will become ill or die. That depends not only on the weather, but also on people’s ability to protect themselves."]},{"k":"p","s":["In Myanmar, though, widespread hardship does not mean equal risk."]},{"k":"p","s":["After years of conflict, displacement and unreliable electricity, extreme heat will deepen existing inequalities. The ",["International Federation of Red Cross and Red Crescent Societies (IFRC)","https://www.ifrc.org/document/heat-through-eyes-most-vulnerable-perceptions-and-pathways-action"]," warns that heat can disrupt electricity, water and healthcare, especially where conflict has damaged infrastructure. The ",["UNHCR","https://www.unhcr.org/sites/default/files/2024-11/no-escape-unhcr-climate-report-2024.pdf"]," highlights displaced people’s greater climate risks due to inadequate housing and essential services."]},{"k":"p","s":["Myanmar is not alone. Three in four people displaced by conflict live in countries ",["highly exposed to climate hazards","https://www.unhcr.org/media/no-escape-ii-way-forward"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Why extreme heat is especially dangerous in Myanmar"]},{"k":"p","s":["The human body cools itself mainly through sweating. When temperatures and humidity remain high, this process becomes less effective, putting extra pressure on the heart and kidneys. The World Health Organization (WHO) warns that ",["extreme heat can worsen","https://www.who.int/news-room/fact-sheets/detail/climate-change-heat-and-health"]," cardiovascular disease, diabetes, asthma and kidney disease."]},{"k":"p","s":["High nighttime temperatures are particularly dangerous because the body needs cooler conditions to recover. Without relief after sunset, the risk of heat-related illness increases."]},{"k":"p","s":["Myanmar’s electricity supply has deteriorated since the military takeover in February 2021. Power cuts have ",["become more frequent during the dry season","https://www.worldbank.org/en/country/myanmar/publication/in-the-dark-power-sector-challenges-in-myanmar"],", when falling hydropower reservoir levels reduce electricity generation while demand for cooling rises."]},{"k":"p","s":["The pressure emerged early this season. Starting Oct. 5, the Ministry of Electric Power and Energy introduced ",["rotating power cuts","https://elevenmyanmar.com/news/power-to-be-distributed-on-rotational-basis-starting-october-5"],", citing El Niño-related heat that had pushed electricity demand beyond available supply."]},{"k":"p","s":["The consequences go beyond losing access to fans and air conditioning (AC). Electricity is also needed to pump clean water, refrigerate medicines and operate medical equipment. ",["A 2023 US modelling study","https://pubs.acs.org/esthag/article/57/22/8245/399320/How-Blackouts-during-Heat-Waves-Amplify-Mortality"]," found that a multi-day blackout during a heatwave could more than double heat-related deaths."]},{"k":"p","s":["Although the exact impact may differ in Myanmar, this highlights an important point: electricity is a public health resource during extreme heat."]},{"k":"h","s":["Who bears the greatest health risks?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Social epidemiologists identify ",["three ways social disadvantage affects health","https://academic.oup.com/book/26479/chapter/194919341"],": exposure, vulnerability and consequences. All three are evident in Myanmar."]},{"k":"p","s":["First, exposure is unequal. Farmers, construction workers and day labourers often continue working during the hottest hours because losing a day’s income is not an option."]},{"k":"p","s":["Wealthier households, meanwhile, can invest in solar-powered cooling such as fans or AC to stay safe during grid blackouts. One industry estimate suggests that household solar installations increased from ",["a few hundred in 2019 to around 300,000 in 2025","https://www.reuters.com/sustainability/climate-energy/war-torn-myanmar-embraces-solar-tackle-power-crisis-2025-11-14/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["With the global fuel shock ",["pushing inflation to 24.6% in April 2026","https://www.worldbank.org/en/news/press-release/2026/06/16/myanmar-s-economy-shows-tentative-stabilization-but-fuel-shock-intensifies-pressures"],", that protection is slipping further out of reach for poorer households. Rising heat stress also ",["threatens workers’ livelihoods and productivity","https://www.ilo.org/resource/news/increase-heat-stress-predicted-bring-productivity-loss-equivalent-80"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Second, vulnerability differs. Older people, young children, pregnant women and people with chronic illnesses face greater health risks during extreme heat. WHO estimates that heat-related deaths among people aged over 65 increased ",["by about 85%","https://www.who.int/news-room/fact-sheets/detail/climate-change-heat-and-health"]," between 2000–04 and 2017–21."]},{"k":"p","s":["Third, the consequences depend on access to treatment. Heatstroke requires rapid cooling and medical attention. Survival may depend on access to transport, functioning clinics, medical equipment and electricity. These are precisely the resources that poor and displaced communities are least likely to have."]},{"k":"h","s":["How conflict widens the protection gaps"]},{"k":"p","s":["Conflict does not flatten these inequalities; it sharpens them. As of July 2026, nearly 3.8 million people ",["were internally displaced","https://www.unocha.org/publications/report/myanmar/myanmar-humanitarian-update-no-52-13-july-2026"]," in Myanmar. Many live in temporary shelters with ",["limited access to clean water and healthcare","https://www.unocha.org/publications/report/myanmar/myanmar-humanitarian-update-no-52-13-july-2026"],". Plastic roofs, overcrowding and poor ventilation leave them particularly exposed to extreme heat."]},{"k":"p","s":["Healthcare access is also increasingly difficult. The humanitarian organisation Insecurity Insight recorded ",["at least 1,939 attacks","https://myanmar.un.org/en/318595-myanmar-health-cluster-bulletin-june-2026"]," on healthcare between Feb. 2021 and May 2026. Ongoing fighting and movement restrictions further limit humanitarian organisations’ ability to deliver medical assistance."]},{"k":"p","s":["For an older woman with heart disease living in a displacement camp, the risks are compounded. She has no fan, limited drinking water and no nearby functioning clinic. Her age, illness, gender and displacement each add to her risk."]},{"k":"p","s":["These disadvantages can reinforce one another, an example of ",["intersectionality","https://chicagounbound.uchicago.edu/uclf/vol1989/iss1/8/"],", a concept used by health equity researchers to explain how overlapping social disadvantages drive poorer health."]},{"k":"p","s":["No study has yet measured these combined effects in Myanmar, where weak death registration also makes heat-related deaths difficult to identify and count."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Epidemiologist Geoffrey Rose","https://academic.oup.com/ije/article-abstract/30/3/427/736897"]," argued that the causes of illness in an individual are not necessarily the same as the factors driving disease across a population."]},{"k":"p","s":["In Myanmar, temperature may explain why someone becomes ill on a particular day. But poverty, displacement and electricity shortages explain why entire communities face greater risks."]},{"k":"h","s":["Why heat preparedness may fail"]},{"k":"p","s":["The military-backed government has begun ",["opening heat shelters","https://elevenmyanmar.com/news/yangon-opens-over-600-heat-shelters-to-counter-super-el-nino-threat"]," in Yangon. But a shelter only protects people who trust it and feel safe enough to reach it."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Young people have been seized","https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c680zlny0gk4o"]," at checkpoints and in public places under the military’s conscription law. Displaced communities have also faced military attacks, including reported ",["airstrikes on displacement camps in Rakhine State","https://www.reuters.com/world/asia-pacific/myanmar-military-airstrikes-rakhine-displacement-camps-kill-eight-rebel-group-2026-10-05/"],". For people living in areas affected by military operations, travelling to an officially designated shelter may itself involve risks."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is also a political and administrative challenge: ",["no single authority","https://thediplomat.com/2026/07/does-myanmar-still-have-one-government-to-recognize/"]," controls all of Myanmar. Ethnic armed organisations and resistance groups administer large parts of the country. Yet most heat plans assume a single government that issues warnings and runs clinics. A plan delivered through the military-backed government alone is unlikely to reach many communities."]},{"k":"p","s":["As the climate warms, Myanmar is a preview for other conflict-affected countries such as Sudan and Yemen, where stronger heat is arriving just as protections are falling apart. Even in a crisis, suffering is not shared equally, and treating crisis-hit populations as one group hides those most at risk. The heat is shared; the harm is not."]}],"chars":6732},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/australia":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"018a991fa3ed890077bed81bb54c583b49cf3caf476ecca5d782faf50a9f3e56","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/australia","bytes":75872,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Australia travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-02-21T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-03-19T14:06:09+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Global travel impacts due to escalation in the Middle East"]},{"k":"p","s":["Escalation in the Middle East has caused widespread travel disruption, including airspace closures, delayed and cancelled flights."]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel plans may be affected, even if your destination is not in the Middle East. Before you travel:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check travel advice for any countries or territories you are transiting through"]},{"k":"li","s":["check for the latest updates from your airline or tour operator"]},{"k":"li","s":["review your travel insurance policy for coverage"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local and international media for the latest information and sign up for travel advice email alerts"]},{"k":"h","s":["Bushfires in Australia"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a higher risk of bushfires in Australia during the spring and summer seasons, from October to February. For advice, visit the bushfires section on the ",["safety and security page","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/australia/safety-and-security#bushfires"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/australia/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of the current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Australia set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Australian High Commission in the UK","https://uk.embassy.gov.au/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Australia, your passport must be valid for the length of your planned stay."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re travelling through or transiting another country on your way to or from Australia, check the entry requirements for that country. Many countries require at least 6 months validity remaining on your passport, even if you’re just in transit and do not pass through immigration."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["British- Australian dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re a British-Australian dual national, you must leave and enter Australia on your Australian passport. You could face difficulties and delays if you do not. See ",["Australian government advice for dual nationals","https://smartraveller.gov.au/guide/dual-nationals.html"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have a visa to visit Australia."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for a visa"]},{"k":"p","s":["British citizens can usually get the following types of electronic visitor visa:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["eVisitor visa","https://immi.homeaffairs.gov.au/visas/getting-a-visa/visa-listing/evisitor-651#Overview"]," – there is no visa application charge or service fee"]},{"k":"li","s":[["Electronic Travel Authority (ETA)","https://immi.homeaffairs.gov.au/visas/getting-a-visa/visa-listing/electronic-travel-authority-601"]," through the ",["iOS app","https://apps.apple.com/au/app/australianeta/id1527982364"]," or ",["Android app","https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=au.gov.homeaffairs.eta&hl=en_AU&gl=US"]," – there is no visa application charge, but there may be a service fee"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Department of Home Affairs has ",["information on all other types of visas","https://immi.homeaffairs.gov.au/visas/getting-a-visa/visa-finder"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Australia, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"],". See the Australian Department of Health’s ",["information on yellow fever for travellers","https://www.health.gov.au/resources/publications/yellow-fever-fact-sheet"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Australia guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/15/australia#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of Australia","https://www.smartraveller.gov.au/while-youre-away/biosecurity-border"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Quarantine rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["Australia has strict quarantine rules to keep out pests and diseases that could affect plant, animal or human health."]},{"k":"p","s":["You must fill in an ",["Incoming Passenger Card","https://www.abf.gov.au/entering-and-leaving-australia/crossing-the-border/at-the-border/incoming-passenger-card-(ipc)"]," and either:"]},{"k":"li","s":["declare goods considered to be a risk, such as food, animal products and plant material (including wooden articles)"]},{"k":"li","s":["dispose of goods in bins at the airport or seaport"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must also declare if you have ‘been in contact with farms, farm animals, wilderness areas or freshwater streams/lakes etc in the past 30 days’."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Australian authorities X-ray luggage. They inspect, treat and, if necessary, confiscate and destroy items of concern. You can get a heavy fine if you break quarantine."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Department of Agriculture has more information on quarantine rules."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Australia"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorists are likely to try to carry out attacks in Australia."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks could be indiscriminate, including in places visited by foreign nationals. You should be vigilant, keep up to date with local media reports and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["In December 2025, 15 people were killed in an antisemitic terrorist attack at Bondi Beach, Sydney."]},{"k":"p","s":["In April 2024, several people were injured in a terrorist incident at a church in Wakeley, Sydney."]},{"k":"p","s":["See the ",["Australian government’s national terrorism threat level","https://www.nationalsecurity.gov.au/national-threat-level/current-national-terrorism-threat-level"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take precautions to protect yourself from petty crime, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["not leaving your bag or luggage unattended"]},{"k":"li","s":["keeping luggage out of sight in cars"]},{"k":"li","s":["keeping valuables and passport in a hotel safe"]},{"k":"li","s":["leaving copies of important documents with family and friends in the UK"]},{"k":"li","s":["carrying a photocopy of your passport for ID"]},{"k":"li","s":["being particularly careful at night in busy tourist areas"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Scams"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are many different types of scams targeting people in or travelling to Australia, including dating and romance scams, websites offering fake services or building repair scams. You can check current scams or report your concerns about a scam on the ",["government’s scamwatch website","https://www.scamwatch.gov.au/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can reduce the risk of losing your passport by carrying a proof of age card – this could be a driving licence or a student ID. This is accepted ID for many services like opening a bank account or entering licensed premises."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Smoking and e-cigarette laws"]},{"k":"p","s":["Laws on smoking and e-cigarettes (vapes) differ between states. The Australian government is reviewing laws, so the rules may change. You must have a prescription to buy e-cigarettes containing liquid nicotine. There are ",["strict rules on importing vaping goods","https://www.odc.gov.au/importers/importing-vaping-goods-australia"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["In all states it is illegal to smoke in enclosed public spaces. Get local advice on any restrictions, and see ",["smoking and tobacco laws in Australia","https://www.health.gov.au/topics/smoking-vaping-and-tobacco/about-smoking/laws-in-australia"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Alcohol"]},{"k":"p","s":["Some drinks served in bars in Australia can be stronger than those in the UK. Alcohol and drugs can lead to you being less alert, less in control and less aware of your environment."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Australian authorities act against anyone who imports or traffics illegal drugs. Prosecution can lead to a lengthy prison sentence and deportation."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex marriages are legally recognised. Australia is generally open-minded about homosexuality, but there are isolated incidents of homophobic crime. Visit Gay Australia is a useful travel planning resource alongside ",["LGBT+ information from the Australian Human Rights Commission","https://humanrights.gov.au/our-work/lgbti"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Mobile phones"]},{"k":"p","s":["The mobile phone network generally works well in cities and large towns, but coverage elsewhere can be very limited or non-existent. If you’re travelling to remote areas, check with your phone provider about coverage. You can use your UK mobile phone in Australia if global roaming has been activated, but making and receiving calls can be expensive. Many visitors prefer to buy an Australian SIM card on arrival."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use any Telstra public payphone to make free phone calls to Australian numbers. Free wifi is also available at some payphones around the country."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Working holidays"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re in Australia on a working holiday visa, the ",["Fair Work Ombudsman","https://www.fairwork.gov.au/"]," website has information about:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your rights as an employee in Australia"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to report any concerns about unfair or unlawful treatment online – you can also call 131 394"]},{"k":"p","s":["Different tax rules and rates apply to residents and non-residents. Working holidaymakers are usually regarded as non-resident for tax purposes. This means they do not qualify for any tax-free personal allowance on earnings. Get guidance from the ",["Australian Taxation Office","https://www.ato.gov.au/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["information for people working in Australia","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-australia#working-in-australia"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Swimming safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["Rip currents are the main hazard for all swimmers and surfers. They can happen at any beach and can sweep even the strongest swimmer out to sea."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow guidance on ",["beach safety in Australia","https://beachsafe.org.au/surf-safety"]," and tips from ",["Surf Life Saving Australia","https://sls.com.au/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals have been injured diving into water that was too shallow. Make sure there is sufficient depth of water before diving, and always follow warning signs."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Diving and snorkelling safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["Snorkelling accidents can happen and have sometimes been fatal."]},{"k":"p","s":["You are required by law to complete a medical declaration for diving or snorkelling at a resort. For your own health and safety, you must be truthful about any medical conditions you have."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Dangerous wildlife"]},{"k":"p","s":["Australia has many dangerous animal species. There are crocodiles, jellyfish, sharks, venomous insects, spiders and snakes in many parts of the country."]},{"k":"p","s":["See Beachsafe’s ",["information on dangerous marine creatures","https://beachsafe.org.au/surf-safety"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Walking and hiking"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re planning to walk or hike, research the area you’re visiting and prepare for the terrain and weather, including intense heat. It can take hours to get help in an emergency in the bush or national parks. There is advice on bush safety on each state or territory’s government website. See:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["New South Wales","https://www.police.nsw.gov.au/safety_and_prevention/safe_and_secure/outdoors"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Queensland","https://parks.des.qld.gov.au/experiences/bushwalking/walk_safely.html"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Victoria","https://www.police.vic.gov.au/outdoor-and-bush-safety"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Western Australia","https://parks.dpaw.wa.gov.au/know/bushwalking"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Northern Territory","https://pfes.nt.gov.au/emergency-service/public-safety-advice/natural-disaster-advice/heatwaves"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["South Australia","https://www.police.sa.gov.au/your-safety/crime-prevention-and-security/safety-and-security-tips"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Tasmania","https://www.parks.tas.gov.au/?base=5576"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Australia, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in Australia if you remain a temporary overseas visitor. If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"]," or get the ",["1949 version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," as well."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you plan to stay in Australia and have a permanent visa, you can drive using your UK licence for up to 3 months. To continue driving, you must get an Australian licence within this 3-month period."]},{"k":"p","s":["Driving laws and regulations differ in each state and territory. Driving under the influence of alcohol or drugs is illegal. The penalties can be severe. You must always wear a seat belt. See the ",["Australian Road Rules","https://www.ntc.gov.au/laws-and-regulations/australian-road-rules"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You must carry your driving licence and passport when driving. Make sure you have sufficient insurance, including if you borrow a car from a friend or relative."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Hire cars"]},{"k":"p","s":["Hire car companies often have stricter requirements for their customers, such as a year of driving experience, a higher minimum age and holding an IDP."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re hiring a car immediately on arrival, be cautious about driving. You might be jetlagged and tired from your flight. Take regular rest breaks at the many rest stops on the roads."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hire car insurance often does not cover driving on unsurfaced roads. Check your policy before you set off."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road conditions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Australia is known for having large distances between towns and amenities."]},{"k":"p","s":["To reduce your risk:"]},{"k":"li","s":["make sure you have enough water before travelling"]},{"k":"li","s":["tell someone about your plans"]},{"k":"li","s":["check road conditions before starting"]},{"k":"li","s":["stay with your vehicle if it breaks down"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the weather forecast – avoid travelling in extreme heat or severe weather"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sudden storms and strong winds can make driving difficult."]},{"k":"p","s":["Take particular care when driving on unsurfaced roads, 4-wheel-drive tracks and desert or beach roads. Northern Territory Police have warned tourists to stay off unsurfaced tracks in remote areas of Central Australia, following reports of stranded motorists."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving in the outback"]},{"k":"p","s":["Prepare thoroughly if driving in remote outback areas, which can present unexpected hazards. To reduce your risk:"]},{"k":"li","s":["take a roadworthy vehicle fitted with GPS and 2 spare tyres"]},{"k":"li","s":["take good maps and extra food, water and fuel"]},{"k":"li","s":["plan your route carefully and get local advice before you set out"]},{"k":"li","s":["leave your route details and expected time of return with the local tourist authorities, police, your hotel or hostel, or friends and relatives, and let them know when you’ve arrived safely"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving on K’gari (Fraser Island)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Following a number of serious accidents, all vehicles on K’gari (Fraser Island) must not drive faster than 80km/h on beaches and 30km/h in towns. Four-wheel-drive vehicles must have no more than 8 occupants, including the driver. You must store all luggage inside the vehicle."]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid driving at night and be aware of beach hazards like ditches created by the surf. K’gari is remote and emergency services can take many hours to reach an accident. Carry a well-stocked first-aid kit and personal medication as there is no pharmacy on the island. The Queensland government has more ",["information on keeping safe in K’gari","https://parks.des.qld.gov.au/parks/kgari-fraser"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to prepare for and respond to ",["extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Bushfires"]},{"k":"p","s":["Bushfires can occur in any part of Australia, including areas close to towns and cities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Be aware of the risk of bushfires, especially at the height of the Australian summer from November to February. Bushfires can start and change direction and become a risk to life very suddenly."]},{"k":"p","s":["Australia regularly battles devastating bushfires. Previous fires resulted in the loss of lives and property with many residents and visitors advised to evacuate."]},{"k":"p","s":["Australian authorities have a range of online information and apps to help citizens and visitors keep track of weather and bushfire warnings. You should consider downloading weather and emergency information apps from the Australian or State governments:"]},{"k":"li","s":["‘ BOM Weather’ – all-Australia weather forecast and warnings ."]},{"k":"li","s":["‘Hazards near me’ – New South Wales"]},{"k":"li","s":[["‘VicEmergency’","https://emergency.vic.gov.au/prepare/#where-do-i-get-information-in-an-emergency"]," – Victoria"]},{"k":"li","s":[["‘AlertSA’","https://www.alert.sa.gov.au/"]," – South Australia"]},{"k":"li","s":["‘ ",["EmergencyWA’","https://news.dfes.wa.gov.au/media-releases-feature-stories/feature-story-emergency-wa-app/"]," – Western Australia"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re in or near an affected area, follow the advice of local authorities:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Australian Capital Territory Fire and Rescue"]},{"k":"li","s":[["New South Wales Rural Fire Service","https://www.rfs.nsw.gov.au/"]]},{"k":"li","s":["Northern Territory Fire and Rescue Service"]},{"k":"li","s":[["Queensland Fire and Emergency Services","https://www.qfes.qld.gov.au/"]]},{"k":"li","s":["South Australian Country Fire Service"]},{"k":"li","s":["Tasmania Fire Service"]},{"k":"li","s":["Victoria’s Country Fire Authority"]},{"k":"li","s":[["Western Australia Department of Fire and Emergency Services","https://dfes.wa.gov.au/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Bushfires can cause poor air quality and aggravate respiratory conditions. Smoke can accumulate far from a fire, including in urban areas and major cities. If you’re unable to avoid smoke affected areas, state and territory governments monitor air quality and give advice:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["Australian Capital Territory","https://www.health.act.gov.au/about-our-health-system/population-health/environmental-monitoring/monitoring-and-regulating-air"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["New South Wales","https://www.dpie.nsw.gov.au/air-quality"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Northern Territory","https://nt.gov.au/environment/environment-data-maps/air-quality-monitoring"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Queensland","https://apps.des.qld.gov.au/air-quality/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["South Australia","https://www.epa.sa.gov.au/data_and_publications/air_quality_monitoring"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Tasmania","https://epa.tas.gov.au/epa/air/monitoring-air-pollution/real-time-air-quality-data-for-tasmania"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Victoria","https://www.epa.vic.gov.au/EPAAirWatch"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Western Australia","https://www.wa.gov.au/service/environment/environment-information-services/air-quality"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Heatwaves"]},{"k":"p","s":["Extreme heat is a serious risk in Australia. See the Australian Red Cross’s ",["information on heatstroke and heat exhaustion","https://www.redcross.org.au/emergencies/prepare/heatstroke-and-heat-exhaustion/"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Flooding"]},{"k":"p","s":["Heavy rain and tropical cyclones can cause flooding, including flash floods in some areas. You can get flood warnings from the Bureau of Meteorology. Check ",["local media reports","https://www.abc.net.au/emergency/?nw=0"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Significant weather events can happen suddenly. Spillways, flood plains and drains can quickly become submerged."]},{"k":"p","s":["The local authorities may issue stay-at-home or leave-now orders. Always follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["More information can be found on the relevant state and territory websites:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["Australian Capital Territory","https://esa.act.gov.au/be-emergency-ready/floods"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["New South Wales","https://www.ses.nsw.gov.au/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Northern Territory","https://depws.nt.gov.au/water/water-resources/flooding-reports-maps"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Queensland","https://www.getready.qld.gov.au/understand-your-risk/types-natural-disasters/flood"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["South Australia","https://www.ses.sa.gov.au/flood/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Tasmania","https://www.service.tas.gov.au/services/emergencies/emergency-alerts/check-current-flood-warnings"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Victoria","https://www.ses.vic.gov.au/plan-and-stay-safe/emergencies/flood"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Western Australia","https://www.dfes.wa.gov.au/site/flood/overview.html"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["While rare in Australia, earthquakes can happen. Follow the advice of the local authorities and emergency services in the event of a natural disaster."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Tropical cyclones"]},{"k":"p","s":["Tropical cyclones affect some parts of Australia, mainly Queensland, Northern Territory and Western Australia. The cyclone season normally runs from November to April."]},{"k":"p","s":["Monitor local and international weather updates from the World Meteorological Organization and the Australian Bureau of Meteorology."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are in or near an affected area, follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Dust storms"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dust storms happen regularly in Australia, usually only in outback areas. Follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dial 000 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance or medical assistance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Australia","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/15/australia#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Australia","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/15/australia#General_Information"]," including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["dengue"]},{"k":"li","s":["Japanese encephalitis and other insect or tick-borne diseases"]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Australia"]},{"k":"p","s":["While you are in Australia, you can access essential and urgent medical care through the UK-Australia Reciprocal Healthcare Agreement. Find out more about ",["healthcare for UK citizens in Australia","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/uk-reciprocal-healthcare-agreements-with-non-eu-countries#australia"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Essential and urgent hospital treatment is free. There is a charge to visit GPs and receive prescriptions. You can recover some costs through Medicare, Australia’s universal health insurance scheme. You can ",["enrol with Medicare through Services Australia","https://www.servicesaustralia.gov.au/reciprocal-health-care-agreements-visiting-from-united-kingdom?context=22481#a3"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re not covered by reciprocal healthcare arrangements between Australia and the UK, costs of treatment can be high."]},{"k":"p","s":["The standard of healthcare in Australia is very good. UK residents are entitled to limited subsidised health services from Medicare for medically necessary treatment while visiting Australia. These provisions do not apply to non-visitors, for example those studying in Australia. Other exclusions under the reciprocal agreement include pharmaceuticals (unless you’re in hospital), use of ambulance services and medical evacuations, which are very expensive."]},{"k":"p","s":["See more ",["information on medical services in Australia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/australia-list-of-medical-facilitiespractitioners"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Australia"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 000 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Australia"]," and ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Australia"]," in Australia"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Australia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/bereavement-information/australia-bereavement-information"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested in Australia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/australia-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/australia/british-high-commission-canberra"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/australia/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Australia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-australia"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":20760,"change":"Updated information about global travel impacts due to escalation in the Middle East (‘Warnings and insurance’ page)."},"https://theconversation.com/guilfoyle-resigns-as-ambassador-to-greece-adding-to-the-global-vacancies-sapping-us-embassies-294315":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:38Z","sha":"bd3cd33554813f376a2f7e29a539161273563ae940aa99413413bfda42ba0bf0","read":"https://theconversation.com/guilfoyle-resigns-as-ambassador-to-greece-adding-to-the-global-vacancies-sapping-us-embassies-294315","bytes":183412,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Guilfoyle resigns as ambassador to Greece – adding to the global vacancies sapping US embassies","by":[{"n":"Donald Heflin","r":"Executive Director of the Edward R. Murrow Center and Senior Fellow of Diplomatic Practice, The Fletcher School, Tufts University"}],"pub":"2026-10-13T18:02:11Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["The United States is down one more ambassador. On Oct. 13, 2026, it emerged that President Donald Trump had asked Kimberly Guilfoyle, a MAGA loyalist and ex-fiancée of Trump’s son Donald Jr., to ",["resign her position as U.S. ambassador to Greece","https://apnews.com/article/trump-ambassador-greece-guilfoyle-9da9d2e50e18bccc38946404c1ca756f"],", a NATO ally. It follows allegations that the Trump adviser turned diplomat pushed for a Republican donor to ",["pay off her six-figure American Express bill","https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/guilfoyle-amex-donor-100-000-0e02cdc3"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Guilfoyle later confirmed that she would comply with the request ",["and resigned","https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/13/us/politics/kimberly-guilfoyle-resign.html"],". In so doing, Athens became one of a number of U.S. overseas missions with a vacancy at the top. In fact, ",["93 out of 196 U.S. ambassador jobs","https://afsa.org/list-ambassadorial-appointments"]," are currently unfilled."]},{"k":"p","s":["And that is after ",["U.S. senators confirmed 10 new ambassadors","https://www.senate.gov/pagelayout/legislative/one_item_and_teasers/nom_confc.htm"]," before leaving town on Sept. 30, 2026. Among those nodded through before Congress closed for an extended midterm recess were new U.S. ambassadors for Kenya, Nicaragua, Malaysia and Kyrgyzstan."]},{"k":"p","s":["With some of the vacancies the White House has not even sent names to Capitol Hill, despite the second Trump administration being a year and a half into the job. With others, the Senate, which is controlled by the same party as the White House, hasn’t acted on the names put forward. Should the Athens position be added to the list, the reason will be down to potential insufficient vetting or an ill-advised appointing strategy that promotes loyalty over experience."]},{"k":"p","s":["Regardless of the reason, as a ",["former ambassador and an expert in the process of diplomacy","https://sites.tufts.edu/murrowcenter/leadership/"],", I find the current vacancies concerning. Among those embassies still without a top person in place are key partners for the U.S. – countries that Washington needs to achieve its security, economic and strategic objectives."]},{"k":"p","s":["What makes these vacancies more worrying, in my view, is that they come amid other concerning developments in the State Department’s staffing of embassies."]},{"k":"h","s":["Politicizing diplomacy"]},{"k":"p","s":["Chief among them are the ",["high percentage of politically appointed ambassadors","https://www.washingtonpost.com/national-security/2026/08/06/trump-fills-ambassador-posts-with-more-donors-loyalists-than-any-recent-president/"]," relative to positions filled by career diplomats – that is, senior foreign service officers, usually with at least 20 years of diplomatic experience."]},{"k":"p","s":["Though many countries send politicians abroad as ambassadors, America’s diplomatic service is unique in two ways. The percentage of U.S. ambassadors who are political appointees – those who haven’t followed a career civil service path – is ",["higher than comparative countries","https://doi.org/10.1093/ia/iiae116"]," across the world. Second, those political appointees are ",["often donors with little to no government experience","https://theconversation.com/trumps-insistence-on-personal-loyalty-from-ambassadors-could-crimp-us-foreign-policy-273087"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The practice has existed for decades, but in recent years the ",["number of political appointees has increased","https://afsa.org/appointments-barack-obama"],". During the Obama administration, the percentage of political appointees was around 30%. The number rose to around 40% in the first Trump administration and the subsequent Biden administration."]},{"k":"p","s":["But in Trump’s second term, some ",["80% of names the White House has sent","https://afsa.org/appointments-donald-j-trump-2nd-term"]," to the Senate have been political."]},{"k":"p","s":["And many of the people Trump has put forward don’t appear to have the credentials usually associated with holding important diplomatic positions. Rather, ",["many are friends, associates or donors","https://www.washingtonpost.com/national-security/2026/08/06/trump-fills-ambassador-posts-with-more-donors-loyalists-than-any-recent-president/"]," to Trump, often with little overseas experience or knowledge of the country they are going to."]},{"k":"p","s":["Lee Lipton, ",["ambassador to a key ally in the Philippines","https://ph.usembassy.gov/ambassador-lee-lipton/"],", is owner of a restaurant in Palm Beach – Florida Benny’s on the Beach – a member of Trump’s Mar-a-Lago Club and a contributor to his political campaign."]},{"k":"p","s":["The system of political appointees has always had an element of handing ambassadorships to friends and supporters. But what has changed under Trump is the range of positions now available. In the past, ambassadors to key countries like Chile, Israel, Peru, the Philippines, Turkey and Egypt, for example, have almost always been career appointees. This has changed under the second Trump administration."]},{"k":"p","s":["Appointing noncareer diplomats to small, faraway nations has the additional problem that the chosen individual may not actually spend much time there. The rule of thumb has long been that ambassadors should spend no more than one month every year back in the United States. But that is compromised if a noncareer diplomat with expansive business ties in the U.S. is selected."]},{"k":"h","s":["The role of a deputy"]},{"k":"p","s":["A closely related problem is the State Department’s handling of an ambassador’s second in command, their ",["deputy chiefs of missions","https://afsa.org/current-deputy-chiefs-mission"]," – DCMs for short – under Secretary of State Marco Rubio."]},{"k":"p","s":["During Trump’s first term in the White House, politically appointed ambassadors were often ",["encouraged to swap out the DCMs","https://theconversation.com/trumps-insistence-on-personal-loyalty-from-ambassadors-could-crimp-us-foreign-policy-273087"]," they inherited from their predecessors. It meant going through a long hiring process, leaving those key jobs unfilled for months."]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2025, the State Department went further, canceling the assignments of senior officers ",["en route to take up embassy jobs","https://www.nbcwashington.com/news/national-international/trump-removes-nearly-30-career-diplomats-from-ambassadorial-positions/4032589/"]," and opening a new hiring process."]},{"k":"p","s":["It formed part of a Trump purge of what many MAGA Republicans ",["characterized as a “deep state” civil service","https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/dec/23/trump-administration-recalls-30-ambassadors-promote-loyal-diplomats"],". The reality is that DCMs ",["fill a critically important role","https://diplomaticacademy.us/2024/12/29/advice-for-political-ambassadors/"]," in helping political appointees navigate the bureaucracy and implement their policy ideas, as well as raising the occasional reality check."]},{"k":"p","s":["With more politically appointed ambassadors – some of them with no relevant experience – having an experienced DCM can be the difference between success and failure."]},{"k":"h","s":["Looking for other friends"]},{"k":"p","s":["When you put all of these personnel changes together, the result is the degradation of what was once seen as one of the most effective diplomatic services in the world."]},{"k":"p","s":["What makes this potentially more worrying is where the vacancies are. For example, Belarus and Bulgaria, neighbors to Russia and Ukraine, are without U.S. ambassadors. And important countries in the fight against terrorism or in geopolitical hot spots, such as Kuwait, Qatar and Mauritania, are in the same camp."]},{"k":"p","s":["Other countries still without ambassadors include Indonesia, Southeast Asia’s largest nation and the most populous Muslim-majority country in the world; key Middle East ally Egypt and nuclear power Pakistan; and nations the U.S. needs to help manage inward migration, such us Haiti and Guatemala."]},{"k":"p","s":["The problem of absent or inexperienced ambassadors goes both ways. It means Washington may not have a capable diplomatic figurehead in these countries to contact in times of need. There are also fewer avenues for host nations to successfully convey messages back to the U.S. administration."]},{"k":"p","s":["When faced with absent ambassadors, amateurish political appointees and deputy mission chiefs who are very junior or career appointees with short resumes, host countries may conclude that they aren’t seen as important to the U.S. and start looking elsewhere for friends."]},{"k":"p","s":["And the U.S. has hollowed out its ambassadorial corps at a time when it is facing growing international influence by the ",["likes of Russia","https://www.rand.org/nsrd/projects/russian-arms-sales-and-sanctions-compliance.html"],", ",["China","https://www.usglc.org/chinas-growing-influence-is-america-getting-left-behind/"]," and Iran – rival nations hoping to capitalize on a perceived diplomatic void left by Washington."]},{"k":"p","s":["For example, as the U.S. tries to ",["contain Beijing’s influence","https://www.brookings.edu/articles/a-framework-for-u-s-policy-toward-china-2/"]," in the Asia-Pacific region, Fiji, Indonesia and Laos remain without U.S. ambassadors. Similarly, China’s diplomatic relations with Pakistan – a former key security partner for Washington – have grown while the ambassadorial seat in Islamabad remains empty."]},{"k":"p","s":["And former Soviet states including Georgia and Kazakhstan don’t have U.S. ambassadors even as Russia President Vladimir Putin attempts to consolidate Moscow’s regional influence."]},{"k":"p","s":["In large areas of the world, such as Africa and the Pacific region, and in important areas of policy, the lights may be on in U.S. embassies, but nobody’s home. And that is a distinct problem for national security and strategic interests."]},{"k":"p","s":["This is an updated version of an ",["article originally published","https://theconversation.com/missing-ambassadors-inexperienced-appointees-is-washington-dropping-the-diplomatic-ball-293487?notice=Article+has+been+updated."]," on Oct. 7, 2026."]}],"chars":7639},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/indonesia":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"100d689c648cb2c627857cc17cf8642871eee78681ae273c5ae54eae190ccfbb","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/indonesia","bytes":99600,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Indonesia travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-11T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-09-18T11:54:47+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Volcanic eruptions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Volcanic eruptions occur frequently across Indonesia. In the event of a volcanic eruption, follow the latest advice issued by the local authorities, including on areas to avoid, exclusion zones and actions to take if air quality is affected."]},{"k":"p","s":["For more details, see ",["Extreme weather and natural disasters","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/indonesia/safety-and-security#extreme-weather-and-natural-disasters"]," on the Safety and security page."]},{"k":"h","s":["Global travel impacts due to escalation in the Middle East"]},{"k":"p","s":["Escalation in the Middle East has caused widespread travel disruption, including airspace closures, delayed and cancelled flights."]},{"k":"p","s":["Commercial options to leave Indonesia remain available, but your travel plans may be affected, even if your destination is not in the Middle East.Before you travel:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check travel advice for any countries or territories you are transiting through"]},{"k":"li","s":["check for the latest updates from your airline or tour operator"]},{"k":"li","s":["review your travel insurance policy for coverage"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local and international media for the latest information and sign up for travel advice email alerts"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/indonesia/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of the current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Indonesia set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Indonesian Embassy in the UK","https://kemlu.go.id/london/en"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Indonesia, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive and have at least 2 blank pages."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have a visa to visit Indonesia."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can get a ",["30-day visa on arrival (VOA)","https://evisa.imigrasi.go.id/"]," for:"]},{"k":"li","s":["tourism"]},{"k":"li","s":["visiting family or friends"]},{"k":"li","s":["some business activities and official meetings"]},{"k":"li","s":["buying goods"]},{"k":"li","s":["official government visits"]},{"k":"p","s":["The VOA is not suitable for all business activities, volunteering, influencer work, or creating commercial online content. If you plan to create sponsored social media content, work as an influencer, or produce online content for commercial purposes while in Indonesia, you may need a different type of visa."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check which visa you need on the ",["Indonesian immigration website","https://www.imigrasi.go.id/wna/permohonan-visa-republik-indonesia"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The VOA costs 500,000 Indonesian rupiah and can be paid by cash or card. It is valid for single entry only."]},{"k":"p","s":["To get a VOA, your passport must meet Indonesia’s entry requirements, and you must have proof of your onward or return journey. Most of the ",["main airports and seaports","https://kemlu.go.id/london/en/news/18631/visa-on-arrival-voa-for-foreign-travellers"]," issue VOAs."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can also apply online for a visa before you travel using the ",["Indonesian immigration website","https://evisa.imigrasi.go.id/"],". Apply at least one week before you leave. You can choose from several visa options, including multiple-entry visas and 60-day visas."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure your visa is approved before you arrive in Indonesia. If it is not approved before you travel, you may only be able to get a 30-day VOA. A visa approved after you enter Indonesia is not valid and you could face penalties for overstaying."]},{"k":"hs","s":["All Indonesia Declaration Form"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before travelling to Indonesia, fill out the online customs and health declaration on the ",["All Indonesia arrival card website","https://allindonesia.imigrasi.go.id/"]," or app within 72 hours of arrival. The All Indonesia arrival card is a service free of charge and travellers should avoid accessing alternative websites or email links that request payment for this service."]},{"k":"p","s":["After completing the form, you can also use the All Indonesia app to apply for a visa."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Extending your visa or residence permit"]},{"k":"p","s":["The 30-day visa can be extended once, for another 30 days, at any immigration office within Indonesia. If you applied online, you can get the extension on the ",["Indonesian immigration website","https://evisa.imigrasi.go.id/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you extend your visa within the initial 30 days to avoid an overstay fine of 1 million rupiah a day."]},{"k":"hs","s":["KITAS extension (stay or work permit)"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re a KITAS holder with an expired stay permit, you can apply for an extension from outside Indonesia through a sponsor. The sponsor must submit the application to the immigration office attaching a copy of your passport and proof of your departure from Indonesia. The application is submitted without biometric sampling. The sponsor must report your arrival within 30 days."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Visa scams"]},{"k":"p","s":["Beware of visa scams by fake visa agents who, having taken your money, may fail to provide a visa or supply the wrong visa. This could result in you overstaying and getting a fine of 1 million rupiah a day, plus possible deportation and a re-entry ban. Use the ",["Indonesian immigration website","https://evisa.imigrasi.go.id/"]," to get or extend your visa."]},{"k":"p","s":["Visa scams are increasing in Indonesia. Some travellers have lost significant amounts of money. Others have been deported despite paying a large fee to an agent to get the correct visa or extension."]},{"k":"p","s":["Travellers are advised to use only the official government links provided via the FCDO travel advice to reduce the risk of engaging with fraudulent services."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Not following visa conditions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Using the wrong type of visa, or staying in Indonesia after your visa expires, is taken very seriously. It can lead to prosecution, detention and deportation at your own cost. The cost of overstaying your visa is one million rupiah a day."]},{"k":"p","s":["If your visa will expire while you are in hospital or in detention, contact Indonesian Immigration before it expires to avoid any overstay fines."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can find more ",["information about visa overstays, deportation","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/indonesia-visa-overstay-and-deportation"]," and how the British Embassy in Jakarta can help in these situations."]},{"k":"h","s":["Registering with the police"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you stay in private accommodation in Indonesia, you must register your presence with the local police at the nearest police station. You could be fined 5 million Indonesian rupiah if you do not register. If you’re staying in a hotel, you will be registered automatically."]},{"k":"h","s":["Bali tourist levy"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Bali provincial government has introduced a tourist levy of 150,000 Indonesian rupiah (approximately £8) for all foreign tourists arriving in Bali. You can pay online or on arrival. See the ",["Bali provincial government website","https://lovebali.baliprov.go.id/"]," for more details."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Indonesia, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Indonesia guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/106/indonesia#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Departure tax"]},{"k":"p","s":["Airport tax is included in the cost of all domestic flights within Indonesia. For some international flights departing Indonesia, airport departure tax might not be included in the price of the ticket. Check with your airline or travel agent before you travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"p","s":["This guide also has safety advice for ",["regions of Indonesia","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/indonesia/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Indonesia"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorists are likely to try to carry out attacks in Indonesia."]},{"k":"p","s":["The threat from Islamist extremism remains high, though the Indonesian authorities continue to disrupt attack planning. Indonesian authorities report multiple arrests of alleged terrorists in the advanced stages of preparation."]},{"k":"p","s":["Indonesian government and law enforcement interests and places of worship are regularly targeted by extremists. Western interests are also at risk. Small-scale attacks occur on a regular basis and further incidents are likely. Attacks could be indiscriminate, including in places visited by foreign nationals. Potential targets include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["beach resorts"]},{"k":"li","s":["hotels, bars and restaurants"]},{"k":"li","s":["markets and shopping malls hosting major international brand outlets"]},{"k":"li","s":["tourist attractions"]},{"k":"li","s":["places of worship"]},{"k":"li","s":["foreign embassies"]},{"k":"li","s":["polling stations"]},{"k":"li","s":["ferry terminals and airports"]},{"k":"p","s":["There’s a heightened risk on and around:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Christmas, New Year and Easter"]},{"k":"li","s":["Chinese New Year"]},{"k":"li","s":["Nyepi (Balinese New Year)"]},{"k":"li","s":["Islamic celebrations and holidays such as Ramadan"]},{"k":"li","s":["national and local elections"]},{"k":"li","s":["presidential inaugurations"]},{"k":"li","s":["Independence Day (17 August)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow the advice of the local authorities, and stay alert in crowded places and at large gatherings."]},{"k":"p","s":["Recent attacks include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["in 2022, a suicide bomber attacked a police post on Jalan Astana Anyar, in Bandung, West Java, killing one and injuring 8 people"]},{"k":"li","s":["in 2021, there was a suicide attack outside the Catholic Cathedral Church at JaIan Kajaolalido, Makassar"]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["The political situation in Indonesia is stable. However, elections, internal and external developments, including in the Middle East, can trigger protests or unrest."]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid all protests, demonstrations and student and political rallies as they can become violent without warning."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sexual assault"]},{"k":"p","s":["Reported cases of rape and sexual assault are high in Bali and Lombok. Be alert when out at night, and avoid areas that are poorly lit."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you call a taxi, use only registered companies, such as Bluebird, Silverbird or Express, and check the driver’s identity. If you book with a mobile app, check the driver is the same as the person on the app, and share your journey with a friend using the app. Be wary of drivers claiming to be registered with app companies and trying to pick up passengers on the street."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Drink spiking"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been reports of drink spiking linked to sexual assault in Bali, Lombok and the Gili Islands."]},{"k":"p","s":["Watch your drinks being prepared, and do not leave them unattended. Do not accept drinks from strangers at clubs or parties."]},{"k":"p","s":["Tourists have been assaulted or robbed after taking visitors to their hotel rooms, and in some cases have found that their drinks were spiked."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Be aware of the risk of street crime such as bag-snatching and pickpocketing, particularly in busy tourist areas. There are often reports of bag-snatching in Bali. Conceal your bag as much as possible to reduce the risk. Carry only essential items and take care of your passport and bank cards."]},{"k":"p","s":["Beware of thieves on public transport and at transport hubs. If you’re travelling by car, keep doors locked while driving."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Scams"]},{"k":"p","s":["Credit card fraud is common. Do not lose sight of your card during transactions. Criminals sometimes place a fake telephone number on ATMs advising customers to report problems so they can fraudulently ask for card details."]},{"k":"p","s":["Unlicensed money changers may short-change you. Only use licensed currency exchanges, identified by a Bank of Indonesia logo and a QR code. Open the code to check the name of the business and its operating licence."]},{"k":"p","s":["There has been a rise in the number of scams at tattoo parlours, nail salons and spas in Bali. Take care when choosing your provider and agree fees in advance."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Alcoholic drinks and drugs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Drinks served in bars can be stronger than those in the UK, usually because the measures of spirits are larger. In some cases, excessive drinking and taking drugs has resulted in accidents, injuries, robbery, assaults and lost travel documents. Some British nationals have suffered psychiatric problems caused by alcohol, drugs and a lack of sleep. Drink responsibly and be aware of your limits."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Methanol poisoning"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been deaths and cases of serious illness caused by alcoholic drinks containing methanol in Indonesia."]},{"k":"p","s":["Methanol poisoning cases have resulted from drinks purchased in licensed bars, shops and hotels in tourist areas. Criminal gangs make counterfeit replicas of well-known alcohol brands and these could contain high amounts of methanol."]},{"k":"p","s":["Even small amounts of methanol can kill. It is not possible to identify methanol in alcoholic drinks by taste or smell. See ",["Travel Aware Spiking and methanol poisoning","https://travelaware.campaign.gov.uk/spiking-and-methanol-poisoning/"]," for information about how to reduce the risks."]},{"k":"p","s":["Seek urgent medical attention if you or someone you are travelling with show the ",["signs of methanol poisoning","https://travelaware.campaign.gov.uk/spiking-and-methanol-poisoning/"]," after drinking."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Ramadan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ramadan is a holy month for Muslims. The dates vary by year and country. Ramadan in Indonesia is from 19 February to 20 March 2026. During this time, do not:"]},{"k":"li","s":["eat, drink, smoke or chew gum in public in the daytime, including in your car"]},{"k":"li","s":["play loud music or dance"]},{"k":"li","s":["swear in public"]},{"k":"p","s":["Get more advice when you arrive from your tour guide, hotel or business contacts."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check opening hours of shops and restaurants"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware that if hotels and restaurants are providing food or drink in fasting hours, they may separate you from Islamic guests, for example with screens"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow local dress codes – clothing that does not meet local dress codes may cause more offence at this time"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware that driving may be erratic, particularly when people are trying to get home at dusk"]},{"k":"li","s":["be patient and show tolerance"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Balinese New Year"]},{"k":"p","s":["Balinese New Year (‘Nyepi’) is on 19 March 2026. During this time, local custom requires that all people in Bali observe a day of silence by staying indoors, turning off lights, and making no noise. Ngurah Rai International Airport is closed for the entire day. However, emergency services and hospitals are allowed to operate."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must always carry your passport or stay permit (such as KITAS or KITAP)."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not get involved with illegal drugs in Indonesia. Possession, using, making or trafficking illegal drugs is a serious crime. The Indonesian authorities have a zero-tolerance policy and those caught may face long prison sentences or the death penalty. Legal cases can be lengthy and costly."]},{"k":"p","s":["Cannabis and cannabis-based products, including medicinal cannabis, cannabis-based oils and creams, hemp-based products, CBD, THC, hash and edibles, are illegal in Indonesia. This applies whether it is carried in a bottle, vape, or any other form. The NHS has ",["guidance explaining how cannabis oils differ","https://www.nhs.uk/medicines/medical-cannabis/"]," and the risks they may carry."]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals have been caught and given long prison sentences for drug offences. Criminal groups sometimes pressure people into carrying drugs across borders. Do not allow yourself to be persuaded."]},{"k":"p","s":["Airports in Indonesia have excellent technology and security for detecting illegal items, including cannabis. This is also used to scan the baggage of transiting passengers."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are detained by the police, it is important to understand your rights. The British embassy provides ",["a guide to the legal and detention systems in Indonesia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/indonesia-prisoner-pack"],", but you must follow local laws and regulations. Any payments requested after arrest, that you agree to, are at your own discretion."]},{"k":"p","s":["In some venues drugs may be offered as free samples. Police often raid venues popular with foreigners, especially in Bali. If police suspect drug use, you may be required to take a urine or blood test. A positive result will lead to arrest."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Alcohol laws and bans"]},{"k":"p","s":["The province of Aceh enforces Sharia law. It is the only province in Indonesia to do so and the laws apply to both Muslims and non-Muslims."]},{"k":"p","s":["In Aceh, the consumption, production and distribution of alcohol are all illegal under Sharia law. Punishment following a Sharia court process is public caning."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity is illegal in the province of Aceh under Sharia law. Punishment following a Sharia court process includes public caning, a prison sentence or a fine payable in gold."]},{"k":"p","s":["Across Indonesia, there have been reports of police arresting individuals at LGBT+ events. Some laws and regulations, including those related to pornography and prostitution, have been applied in a way that discriminates against the LGBT+ community."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should exercise caution and discretion, particularly in public spaces."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Gambling"]},{"k":"p","s":["In the province of Aceh gambling is illegal under Sharia law. Punishment following a Sharia court process includes public caning, a prison sentence or a fine payable in gold."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Extra-marital sex"]},{"k":"p","s":["In the province of Aceh, extra-marital sex is illegal under Sharia law and punishable by public caning after a Sharia court process."]},{"k":"p","s":["Indonesia’s new criminal code imposes penalties for cohabitation and sex outside of marriage if certain members of either party’s immediate family file a complaint."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Wildlife, animal products and souvenirs"]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s illegal to buy, sell, kill or capture any protected wild animal or trade its parts without a licence. If you’re caught buying or smuggling illegal wildlife products, you’ll be prosecuted and could receive a prison sentence and a fine."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Indonesia, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You cannot drive using your UK driving licence. You can drive using an International Driving Permit (IDP) issued by the UK. UK nationals who live in Indonesia and have a limited stay permit card (KITAS) can apply for an Indonesian national driving licence."]},{"k":"p","s":["Before driving, riding or hiring any type of vehicle, ensure that you have the appropriate licence to do so. Check you are covered with your travel insurance company."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving conditions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Traffic discipline is very poor and there has been a large increase in moped and motorbike accidents – some fatal – in Bali. Wear a helmet in good condition if you’re riding a motorbike or moped."]},{"k":"p","s":["Foreign nationals involved in even minor traffic violations or accidents may be vulnerable to extortion. Some multinational companies do not allow their expatriate staff to drive in Indonesia. Consider employing a private driver or hiring a car with a driver."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re involved in an accident, you must wait for the police at the scene. If you have concerns for your safety, move to another location. Make sure someone stays to watch your vehicle if it will not drive. Report the accident at a police station and show full co-operation."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sea travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Travelling by boat or ferry can be dangerous as the sea conditions can change rapidly. Safety standards vary between providers. Vessels can be crowded and overloaded and are often poorly maintained."]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel, check the availability of safety equipment such as life jackets and lifeboats. Life jackets suitable for children are not always available so you may need to bring your own. Avoid travelling after dark unless you’re satisfied the vessel is suitably equipped."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high level of ",["piracy and armed robbery against ships","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/sea-river-and-piracy-safety"]," in and around the Sulu and Celebes seas and in the Malacca Straits."]},{"k":"p","s":["Mariners should be vigilant, set up secure areas on board and report all incidents to the coastal and flag state authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Indonesia regularly experiences natural disasters such as severe weather, floods, landslides, volcanic eruptions, earthquakes and tsunamis."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Volcanic eruptions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Indonesia has many active volcanoes. Volcanoes can erupt without warning and have caused damage and loss of life. Local authorities may evacuate communities near an eruption, and exclusion zones can change at short notice"]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with local authorities and news reports for updates on exclusion zones and safety advice before travelling to areas that are prone to volcanic activity."]},{"k":"p","s":["For the latest information check:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Bureau of Meteorology Volcanic Ash Advisory Centre"]},{"k":"li","s":[["MAGMA Indonesia","https://magma.esdm.go.id/v1"]," (only in Bahasa Indonesia language) for daily updates on status and alert levels"]},{"k":"li","s":["National Disaster Management Authority – BNPB (only in Bahasa Indonesia language)"]},{"k":"li","s":["Global Disaster Alert and Coordination System"]},{"k":"p","s":["While near any volcano, you should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["respect exclusion zones"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local media"]},{"k":"li","s":["stay alert and listen to any local warnings"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow the advice of the local authorities, including any evacuation orders"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sometimes valleys beyond local exclusion zones are affected by mud and debris flows. Volcanic ash may fall outside exclusion zones."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ash clouds can affect flight schedules and the operation of regional airports. Check with your airline or travel company for the latest information."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ash plumes and pollutants from volcanoes can affect air quality and have an impact on health. A fitted face mask may provide some protection from airborne particles. To reduce exposure to hazardous gases, stay inside and close doors and windows. Masks will be available in Indonesia – or buy your own before you travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have any pre-existing respiratory conditions, such as asthma, you might be at ",["increased risk of triggering or worsening your symptoms","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/102/volcanoes"],". Make sure you travel with enough of your regular medicines."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Flooding"]},{"k":"p","s":["The rainy season usually runs from October to March. The wet season can be different in Eastern Indonesia, which usually runs from April to August."]},{"k":"p","s":["Flash floods and widespread flooding can occur across Indonesia, damaging infrastructure, and causing injury and loss of life. There are landslides in mountainous and remote areas, but also in some urban areas/cities, especially Jakarta, and the island of Bali, can suffer severe localised flooding resulting in major traffic congestion and power outages. The main toll road to Soekarno-Hatta International Airport and other major roads in Jakarta can be affected by flooding."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow and monitor local and international weather updates. ",["BMKG - Meteorology, Climatology, and Geophysics Agency","https://www.bmkg.go.id/"]," can be translated into English."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes and tsunamis"]},{"k":"p","s":["Earthquakes happen regularly. If a major earthquake or landslide occurs close to shore, follow the instructions of local authorities, bearing in mind that a tsunami could arrive within minutes. The Indonesia Tsunami Early Warning Centre issues warnings when a potential tsunami with significant impact is imminent or expected. You can also use the BMKG Multi-Hazard Early Warning System app."]},{"k":"p","s":["The US Federal Emergency Management Agency has advice about what to do before, during and after an earthquake or tsunami."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Wildfires"]},{"k":"p","s":["Wildfires in Indonesia’s forests are most severe during the dry season, usually from April to September. Many fires burn all year in the peat-rich soil."]},{"k":"p","s":["The fires, mostly on Sumatra and Borneo, generate a widespread haze that affects air quality throughout the country."]},{"k":"p","s":["Keep up to date with local information and seek medical advice on precautions. See ",["Health","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/indonesia/health"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["More information is available from the ASEAN Regional Haze Situation."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Scuba diving"]},{"k":"p","s":["Diving school standards are not always as high as in the UK. You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check a dive operator’s credentials"]},{"k":"li","s":["make sure you’re covered by insurance"]},{"k":"li","s":["make sure safety equipment is available on the boat, particularly oxygen"]},{"k":"li","s":["ask about safety precautions, including the ability to transfer divers to a hyperbaric chamber"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have not had any previous diving experience:"]},{"k":"li","s":["ask your dive instructor to explain what cover they offer before signing up"]},{"k":"li","s":["check what to do if something goes wrong, including how to call for help while at sea"]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["This section has safety advice for regions of Indonesia. It only covers regions where FCDO has specific advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/indonesia"]," and ",["safety and security advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/indonesia/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Aceh"]},{"k":"p","s":["Aceh has emerged from a long period of internal conflict. Although violence against foreigners is rare, a British national was abducted in 2013 and there were 3 separate incidents in 2009 targeting foreigners. There have been reports of Sharia (religious) police harassing foreigners."]},{"k":"p","s":["Be alert to the risk of politically motivated violence. Take particular care in remote areas. Keep up to date with local developments and avoid large crowds, especially political rallies."]},{"k":"p","s":["Sharia law is in force in Aceh. See ",["Safety and security","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/indonesia/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Central Sulawesi Province"]},{"k":"p","s":["The political situation in Central Sulawesi Province is unsettled. Take particular care in Palu, Poso and Tentena. Be alert to the risk of politically motivated violence."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is conflict between the Indonesian security forces and terrorists, including attacks on police and civilians in 2021. This conflict is predominantly in the Sigi, Parigi Moutong and Poso regions."]},{"k":"h","s":["Maluku Islands"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Maluku Islands have experienced unrest and violence between different religious and tribal groups. Take particular care in Ambon Island, and also in Haruku Island (Pulau Haruku)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Papua region"]},{"k":"p","s":["Armed Papuan separatist groups are fighting for independence from Indonesia in the region of Papua. Violence has been steadily increasing since 2018. The Indonesian government has a heavy security presence throughout the region especially in Highland Papua and Central Papua provinces and along the border with Papua New Guinea."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are regular armed clashes between Papuan separatist groups (known as the TPNPB-OPM) and government security forces, mainly in the regions of Highland Papua and Central Papua."]},{"k":"p","s":["Clashes have resulted in civilian deaths, including foreign nationals. In 2020, a New Zealand national was shot dead and a number of Indonesian nationals were wounded in a mining facility in Highland Papua Province."]},{"k":"p","s":["In February 2023:"]},{"k":"li","s":["a New Zealand national was kidnapped by a separatist group in Nduga, Highland Papua Province"]},{"k":"li","s":["the TPNPB-OPM issued a statement that foreigners in the Papua region would be targeted"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been several instances of Papuan separatists attacking commercial aircraft that service remote communities from small local airfields, especially in Highland Papua and Central Papua provinces. This includes aircraft which are regularly used for transport by foreign nationals and those working in the region."]},{"k":"p","s":["Political tensions have also led to violent demonstrations in cities across Papua, which have turned violent at short notice. Take local advice to help you avoid possible demonstrations and political rallies. Internet communications might be switched off in areas where demonstrations are planned. Make plans in advance in case you are affected."]},{"k":"p","s":["The security situation in Highland Papua and Central Papua provinces is unpredictable and can change quickly. Take local advice to understand current tensions."]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2022, the Indonesian government passed new legislation to reform the governance and administration of the Papua region. Papua and West Papua have been reorganised into 6 provinces:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Papua"]},{"k":"li","s":["West Papua"]},{"k":"li","s":["Central Papua"]},{"k":"li","s":["Highland Papua"]},{"k":"li","s":["South Papua"]},{"k":"li","s":["Southwest Papua"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have previously travelled to the area, make sure you check the updated map."]},{"k":"p","s":["The UK government has no permanent presence in the region. Support for British nationals is managed remotely from Jakarta. There are limited hospital facilities in the region. If you need emergency medical treatment, you are likely to be medically evacuated to Darwin in Australia."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 118 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Indonesia","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/106/indonesia#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Indonesia","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/106/indonesia"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["poor air quality"]},{"k":"li","s":["Zika virus"]},{"k":"li","s":["malaria"]},{"k":"li","s":["dengue"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Air pollution"]},{"k":"p","s":["Air quality in Indonesia’s major cities can reach levels classed as ‘unhealthy for sensitive groups’ or ‘unhealthy’. You can check current air quality data for Jakarta on the Air Quality Index website."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ash plumes from volcanoes can have an impact on health, particularly for anyone with pre-existing respiratory conditions. If you’re affected, get ",["advice on how to prepare and cope with ash fall","https://www.ivhhn.org/pamphlets.html"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["During the dry season from May to November, widespread wildfires cause smoke haze, which drifts across parts of Indonesia, particularly Riau Islands, central Sumatra and Kalimantan. The haze can cause disruption to local and regional air travel, and the air pollution has an impact on public health. Keep up to date with local information and seek medical advice on appropriate precautions. A regional haze map is available from the Singapore Meteorological Service."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Tap water"]},{"k":"p","s":["Tap water is not safe to drink in Indonesia."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Altitude sickness"]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of Indonesia. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Rabies"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are many street dogs in Bali and elsewhere, and monkeys around temples and tourist areas. Rabies exists in both wild and domestic animals, including pets. Seek immediate medical assistance if you’re bitten or scratched."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["TravelHealthPro explains ",["best practice when travelling with medicines","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Indonesia"]},{"k":"p","s":["The standard of local medical care can be poor and some medical tests cannot be performed reliably. Psychological and psychiatric services are also limited."]},{"k":"p","s":["Good medical care can be expensive. In remote areas, you may not be able to get treatment for serious injuries or illness. Medical evacuation can cost tens of thousands of pounds. Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a list of ",["medical providers in Indonesia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/indonesia-list-of-medical-facilities-and-funeral-directors"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["guidance on healthcare if you’re living in Indonesia","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-indonesia#healthcare"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Indonesia"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 118"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 112"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 110"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually need you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO provides guidance on how to help yourself stay safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Indonesia"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Indonesia"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Indonesia"]," in Indonesia"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Indonesia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/bereavement-guidance-indonesia"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested in Indonesia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/indonesia-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help ",["if you’re a victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if ",["you’re in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you are ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/indonesia/british-embassy-jakarta"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/indonesia/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Indonesia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-indonesia"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":32498,"change":"FCDO no longer advises against all travel to volcanoes in Indonesia and will no longer advise against all travel in the event of future volcanic eruptions. FCDO have added new information about volcanoes in Indonesia, including information from the local authorities who enforce exclusion zones on a "},"https://theconversation.com/pope-leos-trip-is-a-homecoming-to-peru-where-debate-over-liberation-theology-roiled-the-church-during-his-early-years-as-a-priest-294299":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T17:18Z","sha":"f7c142d9d6bfd416ad7379adb26f76e7c02d417d6940e169e5a56f42965fc7b7","read":"https://theconversation.com/pope-leos-trip-is-a-homecoming-to-peru-where-debate-over-liberation-theology-roiled-the-church-during-his-early-years-as-a-priest-294299","bytes":197108,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Pope Leo’s trip is a homecoming to Peru – where debate over liberation theology roiled the church during his early years as a priest","by":[{"n":"Eben Levey","r":"Assistant Professor of History, Rochester Institute of Technology"}],"pub":"2026-11-06T18:52:07Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Pope Leo XIV travels to Latin America on Nov. 6, 2026, with ",["a packed itinerary","https://press.vatican.va/content/salastampa/it/bollettino/pubblico/2026/09/21/0736/01738.html#en"]," that will bring him through Uruguay, Argentina and Peru. It is Leo’s first trip to the region since his elevation to the papacy – and a homecoming for ",["a pope who spent two decades in Peru","https://theconversation.com/the-pope-is-peruvian-how-2-decades-in-south-america-shaped-the-vision-of-pope-leo-xiv-256415"]," and holds Peruvian citizenship."]},{"k":"p","s":["As ",["a historian","https://www.rit.edu/directory/eblgla-eben-levey"]," of ",["Catholicism in the late 20th century","https://doi.org/10.13016/4bla-77sh"],", I couldn’t help but notice that ",["the pope’s plans","https://press.vatican.va/content/salastampa/it/bollettino/pubblico/2026/09/21/0736/01738.html"]," walk a fine line during a fraught political moment in Latin America."]},{"k":"p","s":["Leo plans to meet with the ",["right-wing presidents of Argentina","https://en.mercopress.com/2026/11/03/the-pope-arrives-in-an-argentina-where-bishops-are-among-milei-s-firmest-critics"]," ",["and Peru","https://www.ncronline.org/vatican/vatican-news/pope-leos-latin-america-trip-high-stakes-homecoming"],". He will also visit sites often associated with the progressive wing of the Catholic Church, including Casavalle, one of the ",["poorest neighborhoods","https://www.france24.com/en/live-news/20261101-seen-and-heard-uruguay-neighborhood-places-hopes-in-pope"]," in Uruguay’s capital. In Argentina, where President Javier Milei has ",["drastically cut","https://apnews.com/article/argentina-javier-milei-trump-disabilities-austerity-6d98fb3cecc91fe4f3e3f8800826275e"]," funding for disability services, the pope will go to a Catholic home for disabled people."]},{"k":"p","s":["And in Chiclayo, Peru, where Leo served as a bishop, he will pray at a chapel dedicated to St. Óscar Romero. A Salvadoran archbishop, Romero ",["was assassinated in 1980","https://www.ucpress.edu/books/assassination-of-a-saint/paper"]," after years of speaking out against the human rights violations committed by the ",["U.S.-supported","https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/books/36700/the-massacre-at-el-mozote-by-mark-danner/"]," ",["Salvadoran military","https://www.calmigration.org/learn-chapter/civil-war"],". His ministry was influenced by ",["liberation theology","https://theconversation.com/after-50-years-liberation-theology-is-still-reshaping-catholicism-and-politics-but-what-is-it-186804"],", a controversial movement born in Peru that roiled church politics for decades – including during Leo’s years in Peru."]},{"k":"h","s":["What is liberation theology?"]},{"k":"p","s":["The name itself was coined in a 1968 lecture by ",["Gustavo Gutiérrez","https://www.nytimes.com/2024/10/23/world/americas/gustavo-gutierrez-dead.html"],", a Peruvian theologian and priest. He expanded on his ideas in a 1971 book, “ ",["A Theology of Liberation","https://orbisbooks.com/products/9781626985414?srsltid=AYCX9vIJkIEBTafm65WkZiA2WWXGZFkSkEwMIPHf0HdvB5Xz2kRYparw"],".”"]},{"k":"p","s":["Gutiérrez and like-minded theologians argued that Christians have a moral duty ",["to liberate the oppressed","https://theconversation.com/after-50-years-liberation-theology-is-still-reshaping-catholicism-and-politics-but-what-is-it-186804"],". They saw poverty, violence, racism and discrimination as not just problems but collective sins. While building on earlier Catholic social teachings, these “liberationists” envisioned profound change that went beyond the spiritual care and charitable work of traditional Latin American Catholicism."]},{"k":"p","s":["Catholics ",["inspired by liberation theology","https://press.uchicago.edu/ucp/books/book/chicago/E/bo3631145.html"]," created community organizations and work cooperatives, organized labor unions and fostered other initiatives that sought to measurably improve the lives of the poor. In ",["my own research","https://www.bloomsbury.com/us/liberation-theology-and-the-others-9781793633637/"],", I’ve documented how priests and nuns in rural Mexico helped organize transportation, corn milling and carpentry cooperatives."]},{"k":"p","s":["Gutiérrez also argued that Christians should use Marxist ideas about ",["analyzing society and the economy","https://www.bloomsbury.com/us/pedagogy-of-the-oppressed-9781501314131/"]," to ",["better understand inequality","https://monthlyreview.org/9780853450931/"],". In nations like Peru, ",["which possessed rich natural resources","https://doi.org/10.4324/9780429315060"],", liberationists tailored their economic justice projects to address how international and national companies profited off the low wages of miners and farmers."]},{"k":"p","s":["During the Cold War, however, these ideas led some politicians and church leaders to accuse liberationists of socialism and communism."]},{"k":"p","s":["A minority fringe of liberationists did embrace left-ring radicalism. ",["Christians for Socialism","https://kellogg.nd.edu/space-utopia-christians-socialism-chile"],", for example, argued that liberation ",["meant rejecting capitalism","https://www.cambridge.org/core/blog/2025/12/12/the-chilean-christians-for-socialism-movement-liberationist-third-worldist-and-utopian/"],". Some clergy, although only a handful, even ",["picked up arms","https://www.routledge.com/Camilo-Torres-Priest-Liberation-Theologian-Guerrilla-Fighter/Ginzberg/p/book/9781032990255"]," to fight alongside clandestine left-wing revolutionary groups."]},{"k":"h","s":["A wary pope"]},{"k":"p","s":["This presented a dilemma to the Vatican."]},{"k":"p","s":["In 1891, Pope Leo XIII – ",["the current pope’s namesake","https://theconversation.com/19th-century-catholic-teachings-21st-century-tech-how-concerns-about-ai-guided-pope-leos-choice-of-name-256645"]," – ",["published “Rerum Novarum","https://www.vatican.va/content/leo-xiii/en/encyclicals/documents/hf_l-xiii_enc_15051891_rerum-novarum.html"],",” an encyclical focused on workers’ rights amid the Industrial Revolution. Since then, the Vatican had critiqued the worst excesses of capitalism while also rejecting socialism and communism, which it viewed as godless ideologies."]},{"k":"p","s":["During the 1960s and ’70s, Pope Paul VI generally ",["supported local initiatives by liberationist Catholics","https://www.commonwealmagazine.org/introduction-%E2%80%98commonweal%E2%80%99-and-liberation-theology"],", including some ",["in Chulucanas, Peru","https://www.nybooks.com/online/2026/05/24/the-education-of-pope-leo-xiv/"],", where Leo began his missionary work. Paul appointed and elevated bishops who shared a vision that the church could help empower the poor and alleviate oppression."]},{"k":"p","s":["But the Vatican shifted when the Polish cardinal Karol Józef Wojtyla became Pope John Paul II in 1978. For most of his adult life, Poland had been part of the Soviet bloc, which imposed restrictions on organized religion. A ",["staunch opponent of communism","https://www.anneapplebaum.com/2005/04/06/how-the-pope-defeated-communism/"],", ",["he worried about liberation theology’s","https://time.com/archive/6854086/religion-john-paul-vs-liberation-theology/"]," use of Marxist analysis. So did one of his top Vatican officials, Joseph Ratzinger – the future Pope Benedict XVI."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Vatican began investigating ",["some liberation theologians","https://wipfandstock.com/products/marx-and-the-bible-9781592444854?srsltid=AYCX9vK51gjTntA4LFREX5-quPazIhRZj3zxLHw_WdGvf0hAHqxu3p6B"]," for violations of church teachings. In 1985, for example, Brazilian liberationist theologian Leonardo Boff was ordered to observe a ",["year of silence","https://search.worldcat.org/title/813628776"]," – no publishing, no public speaking – to discipline him for his critique of the church’s hierarchy. Several priests ",["were suspended","https://www.bbc.com/news/world-latin-america-28656661"]," ",["over their work","https://www.americamagazine.org/news/2016/02/23/nicaragua-jesuit-fernando-cardenal-dies-82/"]," in Sandinista Nicaragua."]},{"k":"p","s":["John Paul ordered that the Peruvian bishops begin an investigation of Gutiérrez – above all, over ",["Marxism’s influence on his work","https://www.ncronline.org/news/theology/vatican-doctrinal-czar-liberation-theology-pioneer-reflects-troubles"],". Gutiérrez was ultimately not punished."]},{"k":"p","s":["One factor in his favor may have been his consistent opposition to armed revolution, even before violence raged in Peru from the 1980s into the ’90s. ",["The Shining Path","https://www.dukeupress.edu/Shining-and-Other-Paths"],", a Maoist guerrilla group, was waging a war of terrorism against the Peruvian government, setting off bombs across Peru."]},{"k":"p","s":["Under President Alberto Fujimori, the government escalated existing counterinsurgency operations, often using indiscriminate violence against citizens in the region where the Shining Path emerged. In 2009, Fujimori was convicted of ",["human rights violations","https://academic.oup.com/ijtj/article-abstract/3/3/384/2888395?redirectedFrom=fulltext"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Young priest"]},{"k":"p","s":["Leo has never described himself as a liberationist Catholic. However, his experiences as a priest were ",["indelibly shaped by liberation theology","https://www.nybooks.com/online/2026/05/24/the-education-of-pope-leo-xiv/"],", the Peruvian armed conflict and the church debates that roiled much of Latin America during his years there."]},{"k":"p","s":["Leo, born Robert Prevost, was raised in Chicago. After ordination, his journey as a priest began in Peru, where he landed for missionary work in 1985. The young friar followed in the footsteps of other ",["U.S. Catholic missionaries","https://undpress.nd.edu/9780268029050/maryknoll-catholic-mission-in-peru-1943-1989/"]," who had been serving among Peru’s poor and Indigenous, urban and rural, since the 1940s."]},{"k":"p","s":["Sent to Chulucanas, in Peru’s coastal northwest, Prevost found himself in a region of pastoral experimentation. Since the 1960s, Augustinian missionaries had been ",["working closely","https://www.nybooks.com/online/2026/05/24/the-education-of-pope-leo-xiv/"]," with the community to provide literacy education, discussion groups about poverty and inequality, and workshops to train artisans."]},{"k":"p","s":["These programs were a far cry from the more radical actions of some Catholics who supported liberation theology. Nevertheless, the programs in Chulucanas aimed to empower the Peruvian poor, chipping away at exploitation and low wages on the region’s sugarcane and cotton estates. Like Gutiérrez, many Peruvian Christians believed that the Shining Path ",["drew support because of pervasive poverty and inequality","https://doi.org/10.1179/1462317X13Z.0000000004"],", and that churches could help transform the nation."]},{"k":"p","s":["But the Catholic Church in Latin America was in the midst of another transformation. John Paul gradually appointed ",["conservative bishops","https://www.routledge.com/The-Politics-of-Transnational-Actors-in-Latin-America-Power-from-Afar/Shepherd/p/book/9781138096332"]," across the continent. Experimental pastoral programs lost support, and institutions that trained priests to put liberation theology into action, such as the ",["Regional Seminary of the Southeast","https://doi.org/10.13016/4bla-77sh"]," in Mexico, were shuttered or “reoriented.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["Yet even as the hierarchy shifted conservative, work on the ground among Latin America’s poorest continued apace. From ",["coffee cooperatives in Mexico","https://press.umich.edu/Books/D/Divined-Intervention2"]," to ",["human rights activists","https://doi.org/10.1515/9783111726069"]," across the continent, many programs survived."]},{"k":"h","s":["‘Cease the repression’"]},{"k":"p","s":["Leo’s 2026 itinerary includes multiple stops that speak to this history and on-the-ground pastoral work. The most symbolic, perhaps, is the Capilla San Óscar Romero, located in Chiclayo, the pope’s former diocese."]},{"k":"p","s":["A neighborhood chapel ",["renovated with donations","https://www.latintimes.com/pope-leo-xiv-visit-chiclayo-chapel-600527"]," from Leo’s connections in the United States, it is one of many sites throughout the Americas honoring Catholics who fell victim to right-wing, anti-communist violence. The day before Romero’s assassination, he used his weekly radio address to speak directly to El Salvador’s conscripted soldiers, telling them, “ ",["No soldier is obliged to obey an order counter to the law of God","https://sojo.net/magazine/may-1980/pastors-last-homily"],".”"]},{"k":"p","s":["Leo XIV’s visit to the chapel is for private prayer, not a homily or a speech. Still, I would argue that the soft-spoken pope’s stop will evoke Romero’s message – especially at a time of ",["strikes against suspected drug traffickers","https://apnews.com/article/rubio-peru-drug-trafficking-trump-b625fe79a901799707343ff5dd83b5f4"],", which ",["human rights groups","https://www.hrw.org/news/2025/09/18/us-maritime-strikes-amount-to-extrajudicial-killings"]," have ",["criticized as extrajudicial killings","https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/ck5ye7v88qy7o"],". ",["During his final Mass","https://sojo.net/magazine/may-1980/pastors-last-homily"],", Romero pleaded, “I beseech you, I beg you, I command you in the name of God: Cease the repression!”"]}],"chars":8225},"https://theconversation.com/massive-super-pac-spending-did-not-secure-republican-victories-in-2026-but-it-remains-a-pernicious-influence-in-both-parties-296028":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T17:32Z","sha":"9eeaaffec2a59330b049d5a494cc97159723a995b3b7e71e73a8ffe89ecbfea7","read":"https://theconversation.com/massive-super-pac-spending-did-not-secure-republican-victories-in-2026-but-it-remains-a-pernicious-influence-in-both-parties-296028","bytes":188295,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Massive super PAC spending did not secure Republican victories in 2026, but it remains a pernicious influence – in both parties","by":[{"n":"Robert Boatright","r":"Professor of Political Science, Clark University; Institute for Humane Studies"}],"pub":"2026-11-17T13:39:41Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["It was almost as if all the money didn’t matter."]},{"k":"p","s":["Republican super PACs ",["substantially outspent Democratic ones","https://www.opensecrets.org/outside-spending-2026/by-race"]," in the 2026 midterm elections – particularly in Texas, where Elon Musk spent an astounding ",["US$224 million","https://www.opensecrets.org/outside-spending-2026/top-donors"]," on behalf of Republican Ken Paxton’s Senate campaign."]},{"k":"p","s":["Yet Republicans lost across the board – ",["regardless of whether they had super PAC support","https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/12/opinion/republicans-campaign-money-midterms.html"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Not only did they lose, but the swing toward Democrats was remarkably consistent across the entire country, regardless of how much money was spent or what the fundraising imbalance was."]},{"k":"p","s":["So, do the 2026 election results mean that super PAC spending, which represents the single-largest category of campaign spending in competitive races, doesn’t matter as much as we thought? Do they mean that Americans should worry less about the effect of these super PACs on politics?"]},{"k":"p","s":[["As a political scientist","https://wordpress.clarku.edu/rboatright/"]," who studies campaign spending, I would say no. Here’s why."]},{"k":"h","s":["The limited effects of super PACs in general elections"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Super PACs","https://campaignlegal.org/update/pacs-super-pacs-dark-money-groups-whats-difference"]," are political committees that engage in political advocacy but do not donate money to candidates or directly coordinate their strategies with them. Because of this, there are no limits on what super PACs can spend or on the size of the contributions they can receive."]},{"k":"p","s":["They have ",["limited effects","https://doi.org/10.3982/ECTA22979"]," on general elections. In competitive general election races for the House and Senate, it is usually the case that both candidates have significant funding, so the incremental value of each dollar declines as spending increases."]},{"k":"p","s":["In each election cycle, ",["approximately 90% of voters","https://www.pewresearch.org/politics/2025/06/26/voting-patterns-in-the-2024-election/"]," vote for the same party they did in the previous election. Voters such as these are unlikely to be moved by super PAC advertising."]},{"k":"p","s":["Most importantly, super PAC spending is less efficient than spending by candidates or parties. By law, candidates and parties receive the “ ",["lowest unit charge","https://campaignlegal.org/document/comment-federal-communications-commission-review-lowest-unit-charge-guidance"],",” or LUC, from television networks – that is, they pay the lowest permissible rate for advertising in a particular time slot. Super PACs do not receive the LUC, and thus they can pay ",["two or three times as much","https://www.politico.com/news/2026/08/25/federal-court-tv-advertising-rates-elections-01050099"]," per advertisement."]},{"k":"p","s":["In a broader sense, however, the fact that super PACs cannot legally coordinate with candidates means that they are not able to spend money as wisely as candidates do. Usually, candidates and parties have access to the top consultants, they are likely to have information about what worked in the last election in their state or district, and they often have targeting information about voters."]},{"k":"p","s":["A super PAC could acquire these things, but it cannot acquire them from the candidates themselves. In addition, many super PACs are ephemeral – they are organized to advocate for one particular candidate or set of candidates, and they do not last more than a few months. As a consequence, they do not have the ability to learn from their past efforts."]},{"k":"p","s":["This may have been a particular problem in Texas. The sheer volume of spending by Musk in such a short time frame meant that there was little infrastructure to support his spending – all his super PAC could do was buy a lot of relatively untargeted advertisements."]},{"k":"p","s":["Yet despite their often crudely targeted efforts to help candidates, super PACs still are a pernicious influence in politics for four reasons."]},{"k":"h","s":["1. Super PACs spend a tremendous amount of money"]},{"k":"p","s":["Nearly two-thirds of super PAC spending in 2026 can be traced to only ",["100 people","https://www.opensecrets.org/outside-spending-2026/top-donors"],". These 100 people have very narrow business interests, but few of them are as controversial as Musk. One reason Musk’s massive spending was not helpful was that Paxton’s opponent, ",["James Talarico, made his criticism of Musk","https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/25/us/politics/talarico-musk-texas-senate-paxton-midterms.html"]," a part of his campaign. Most super PAC donors are not as likely to provoke the sort of backlash that may have blunted Musk’s effectiveness in Texas."]},{"k":"p","s":["Without public pushback based on an awareness of a donor’s agenda, this spending can reorient campaigns to be about the idiosyncratic ideas of an unrepresentative group of billionaires. It makes campaigns about something other than what parties, candidates and voters want them to be about. Parties and candidates, in turn, must raise more money than before just to be heard."]},{"k":"h","s":["2. Super PACs shape elections long before November"]},{"k":"p","s":["Super PACs play a major role in primary elections, where voters are choosing among candidates of the same party and cannot simply use a candidate’s party label to choose whom to vote for. Some of the most expensive elections in 2024 and 2026 were primary elections in safe districts where one party was overwhelmingly favored to win the general election."]},{"k":"p","s":["In the 9th District of Illinois, for instance, super PACs spent ",["$9.1 million","https://www.opensecrets.org/state-profiles/illinois/elections?cycle=2026&race_category=house&race_section=outside_spending&race_slug=illinois-district-09&scope=us_congress"]," in the Democratic primary in support of six candidates. Few voters in the 9th District knew how much had been spent, who the groups were, or even what issues motivated these groups until after the election."]},{"k":"p","s":["Super PACs have also increased their spending in ",["nonpartisan municipal elections","https://doi.org/10.1017/9781009877404"],", where there is little advertising or media coverage and therefore voters often have even ",["less information","https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/american-political-science-review/article/who-votes-city-election-timing-and-voter-composition/39CE6B9F0E906228F695248C874C0C36"]," about the candidates or their policies."]},{"k":"h","s":["3. Super PACs can be a vehicle for nefarious schemes"]},{"k":"p","s":["During the 2026 midterm campaign, ",["conservative super PACs in Ohio","https://www.cleveland.com/metro/2026/10/conservative-pac-supplied-25-million-to-group-promoting-ohio-socialist-greg-levy.html"]," and ",["Massachusetts","https://www.wgbh.org/news/politics/2026-10-21/why-is-a-pro-mike-minogue-super-pac-targeting-mass-governor-candidate-andrea-james"]," sent out deliberately deceptive mailings highlighting obscure socialist candidates, aiming to siphon votes away from the Democrats these groups were really concerned about."]},{"k":"p","s":["While politics can often be dirty and these mailings were not illegal, they enable the candidates these groups supported to ",["claim they have nothing to do with them","https://www.cnn.com/2026/10/31/politics/alaska-senate-race-pac-spending-invs"],". A candidate, a party or an established interest group has a reputation to protect, and voters can hold them accountable for the quality of their campaigns. Super PACs do not have to worry about this because they do not appear on the ballot, and they do not have members or stockholders who can put pressure on them."]},{"k":"h","s":["4. Super PAC spending can affect how legislators behave"]},{"k":"p","s":["Even legislators with very safe seats must constantly worry about whether one vote, or one statement, might cause someone to spend a large sum of money against them. Many legislators cast votes ",["they know their constituents will dislike","https://doi.org/10.1017/9781108768375"]," in order to avoid antagonizing groups that might spend against them in their primary."]},{"k":"h","s":["It’s legal, if deplored, by the public"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Most Americans","https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2023/10/23/7-facts-about-americans-views-of-money-in-politics/"]," want limits on super PAC spending."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Many Democratic candidates in 2026","https://www.brookings.edu/articles/electability-over-ideology-takeaways-from-the-2026-primaries/"]," called for campaign finance reforms. It is tempting to believe that the new Democratic majorities in Congress will do something to rein in super PACs. There are many obstacles to doing so, however."]},{"k":"p","s":["For one, the Supreme Court is unlikely to change its views on the legality of independent spending. ",["The justices have decreed it is speech","https://www.oyez.org/cases/2008/08-205"],", and they see no constitutional restraint on this kind of speech."]},{"k":"p","s":["While voters support campaign finance reform, they ",["rarely list it as their top priority","https://press.uchicago.edu/ucp/books/book/chicago/C/bo51203857.html"],". And although Republicans benefited more from super PAC spending in 2026 than Democrats, many Democratic candidates have been dependent on it as well. The Democrats’ comfortable majority may make it easier than before for Democrats to receive more super PAC support."]},{"k":"p","s":["Although super PAC support did not propel Republicans to victory in 2026, the real danger of super PACs is that most politicians, regardless of party, have become dependent upon them."]}],"chars":7227},"https://theconversation.com/black-michiganders-helped-push-abdul-el-sayed-to-victory-but-the-numbers-show-he-was-less-popular-with-this-key-voting-bloc-than-some-other-democratic-candidates-289777":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T17:32Z","sha":"ccb720b87c9872908c0546f14f94eb12f356e28d43022acc59bccc68cd069798","read":"https://theconversation.com/black-michiganders-helped-push-abdul-el-sayed-to-victory-but-the-numbers-show-he-was-less-popular-with-this-key-voting-bloc-than-some-other-democratic-candidates-289777","bytes":188207,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Black Michiganders helped push Abdul El-Sayed to victory – but the numbers show he was less popular with this key voting bloc than some other Democratic candidates","by":[{"n":"Christine Slaughter","r":"Assistant Professor of Political Science, Boston University"}],"pub":"2026-11-05T20:56:31Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Progressive Abdul El-Sayed’s ",["victory in Michigan’s U.S. Senate race","https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/democrat-abdul-el-sayed-wins-election-to-u-s-senate-from-michigan"]," was one of the most-watched contests in the 2026 midterm elections."]},{"k":"p","s":["As the results for this race came in, I had my eye on one demographic: Black voters. I am a ",["political scientist","https://www.bu.edu/polisci/profile/christine-slaughter/"]," who studies Black political behavior. My research has been ",["published in numerous journals","https://scholar.google.com/citations?hl=en&user=7TP1C6cAAAAJ&view_op=list_works&sortby=pubdate"],", as well as in my forthcoming book, “Black Resilience,” which examines Black voters’ political participation."]},{"k":"h","s":["Wayne County voters"]},{"k":"p","s":["The support of Black voters for El-Sayed was not a given. In the August primary, ",["62% of Detroit voters","https://detroitmi.gov/sites/detroitmi.localhost/files/2026-08/OFFICIAL%20Election%20Summary%20Report%20-%20August%20Primary%202026.pdf"]," chose U.S. Rep. Haley Stevens over El-Sayed. ",["Many pundits predicted","https://www.bridgedetroit.com/detroit-is-key-to-abdul-el-sayeds-senate-bid-but-he-faces-deep-divides/"]," it would be difficult for El-Sayed to gain support in Detroit, ",["which is about 75% Black","https://www.census.gov/quickfacts/detroitcitymichigan"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["After the primary, El-Sayed made overtures by ",["sharing his plans","https://abdulforsenate.com/2026/09/thrive-transforming-housing-resources-infrastructure-value-economic-opportunities/"]," to improve the lives of Black Americans, which included supporting the growth of minority-owned businesses, creating more affordable housing, eliminating food deserts and expanding the ",["Rx Kids cash assistance program","https://theconversation.com/im-a-pediatrician-in-michigan-who-created-rx-kids-one-of-the-nations-largest-anti-poverty-programs-heres-what-ive-learned-about-how-medical-schools-can-improve-community-health-277064"]," nationwide."]},{"k":"p","s":["About 91.8% of Detroit voters supported El-Sayed in the general election, ",["according to the city’s unofficial results","https://app.enhancedvoting.com/results/public/city-detroit-mi/elections/_20261027152933"],". Detroit City Clerk Janice Winfrey said ",["209,924 residents voted in the 2026 midterms","https://www.freep.com/story/news/politics/elections/2026/11/04/michigan-record-turnout-2026-midterms-blue-wave/92609483007/"],", up about 21% from the 2022 midterm elections. For the 2024 presidential election, 247,770 city residents cast a ballot."]},{"k":"p","s":["In fact, El-Sayed received ",["70.6% of Wayne County votes","https://apnews.com/projects/elections-2026/michigan-us-senate-results/"],", which includes Detroit. In 2024, Kamala Harris received ",["62.7% of the vote in Wayne County","https://apnews.com/projects/election-results-2024/michigan/?r=0"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Statewide support is holding steady"]},{"k":"p","s":["In the 2024 presidential election, Michigan’s ",["Democratic vote share fell to 48.3%","https://apnews.com/projects/election-results-2024/michigan/?r=0"],", ",["from 50.6% in 2020","https://ballotpedia.org/Michigan_election_results,_2020"],", as the state went for Donald Trump instead of Democratic nominee Harris."]},{"k":"p","s":["Despite their ideological differences, Sen. Elissa Slotkin and El-Sayed drew ",["similar support among Black voters.","https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2026-elections/michigan-senate-results"]," In 2024, Slotkin – a moderate Democrat – won 48.6% of the vote, a small margin over Mike Rogers, who was the Republican candidate in that race. In 2026, El-Sayed defeated Rogers statewide by a substantially wider margin, winning 52% of the vote."]},{"k":"p","s":["In other words, these early election results do not indicate whether Black voters embraced El-Sayed’s progressive platform or simply voted for the Democratic candidate. Voters may have been rejecting Republican Party politics or expressing anger toward Trump over pocketbook issues."]},{"k":"p","s":["Researchers from Michigan State University found that precincts with more than 80% of Black voters ",["supported Democratic statewide candidates","https://ippsr.msu.edu/sites/default/files/mappr/ElectoralSize%26Support.pdf"]," over Republicans at a rate of 92% to 94% during the 2024 general election, which is only slightly lower than the 94% to 95% levels observed in similar precincts during the 2020 contest between Trump and Joe Biden."]},{"k":"p","s":["Even while Black voters overwhelmingly support Democrats, small shifts in their support and turnout can influence the outcome of close and competitive races. These shifts may help explain differing outcomes, including El-Sayed’s victory in 2026 and Harris’ defeat there in 2024."]},{"k":"p","s":["While Black voter support for El-Sayed was high, estimated at around ",["86% statewide","https://michiganchronicle.com/despite-doubts-these-detroit-voters-say-theres-excitement-for-abdul-el-sayed/"],", Gov. Gretchen Whitmer’s support among Black voters was about 94% in the 2022 gubernatorial race, according to an ",["ABC exit poll","https://abcnews.com/Elections/michigan-exit-polls-2022-us-governor-election-results-analysis"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Similarly, preelection polling indicated that Jocelyn Benson, the Democratic nominee for governor, polled ",["more favorably among nonwhite voters compared to El-Sayed","https://maristpoll.marist.edu/polls/midterm-elections-in-michigan-october-2026/"],". ",["NBC exit poll data","https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2026-elections/michigan-senate-results"]," shows that 86% of Black voters in Michigan supported El-Sayed, while ",["90% supported Benson","https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2026-elections/michigan-senate-results"],", who won the governorship over Republican John James."]},{"k":"h","s":["Historic power and unity"]},{"k":"p","s":["Black voters are often strategic voters who support the candidate they believe best aligns with Black interests, which has usually been the Democratic candidate since the Civil Rights Movement."]},{"k":"p","s":["Generally, Black voters have made their electoral choices based on what’s believed to be best for the group as a whole – a concept described by political scientist Michael C. Dawson as ",["linked fate","https://doi.org/10.2307/j.ctvzxx9d4.6"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, recent research shows that Black social networks and institutions, including churches and civic organizations, reinforce expectations of ",["political solidarity","https://press.princeton.edu/books/hardcover/9780691199511/steadfast-democrats?srsltid=AYCX9vIo-pt1ZijIzpph8UHVplgdt7qREMzFKjFAUBo307f-9LPTnm3q"],". Weaker ties to these networks may lessen the social pressure that encourages Black Americans to participate in politics and support Democratic candidates."]},{"k":"p","s":["Lower participation by Black Americans could lead to elected officials paying less attention to issues important to Black voters, such as ",["affordability and the cost of living, healthcare, and reducing racial discrimination","https://www.lcv.org/media-center/new-poll-ahead-of-midterms-black-and-latino-battleground-voters-rate-climate-a-high-priority-when-tied-to-affordability-and-pollution/"],". If officials assume Black voters will remain loyal to Democrats, they’re under less pressure to win their votes by addressing their concerns."]},{"k":"p","s":["My research has demonstrated that after the 2024 election, ",["Black women in particular felt frustrated","https://doi.org/10.1007/s11109-026-10155-6"]," with the Democratic Party, yet they participated in elections despite these frustrations."]},{"k":"h","s":["An agenda that matters"]},{"k":"p","s":["El-Sayed was part of a field of notable Democratic candidates in this election cycle. For example, Angie Nixon, a state representative in Florida, championed affordability ",["alongside a moratorium on evictions and a universal jobs program","https://19thnews.org/2026/10/angie-nixon-florida-senate-moment/"],", while James Talarico, a ",["former schoolteacher","https://jamestalarico.com/issue/public-education/"]," in Texas, focused on public education."]},{"k":"p","s":["El-Sayed is a former public health official who had not previously held elected office. This may have turned off some Black voters who often ",["value governing experience","https://www.jstor.org/stable/pdf/4122905.pdf"],". El-Sayed advocated for Medicare For All and lowering the costs of gas prices and groceries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Although he doesn’t identify as a democratic socialist, El-Sayed campaigned with several progressive elected officials, such as U.S. Rep. Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez. U.S. Sen. Bernie Sanders ",["endorsed El-Sayed","https://www.commondreams.org/news/abdul-el-sayed"]," on the day he announced his candidacy in 2025. El-Sayed also campaigned with the Black establishment, including U.S. Rep. ",["Jim Clyburn","https://michiganadvance.com/2026/11/02/michigan-democrats-rally-behind-el-sayed-as-stevens-goes-rogue-to-support-rogers/"]," of South Carolina. Former President ",["Barack Obama","https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/24/barack-obama-abdul-el-sayed-michigan"]," spoke at a rally for El-Sayed in Detroit in October 2026."]},{"k":"p","s":["Stevens, who ",["lost the Democratic nomination to El-Sayed","https://bridgemi.com/michigan-politics/michigan-democratic-senate-primary-results-abdul-el-sayed-haley-stevens/"]," in the primary, endorsed Republican Mike Rogers after she attended a service with the Republican candidate at ",["a predominantly Black church in Detroit two days before the election","https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2026-election/haley-stevens-endorses-gop-mike-rogers-michigan-senate-race-el-sayed-rcna606831"],". Stevens’ tactic ",["drew severe backlash","https://www.axios.com/2026/11/01/haley-stevens-democrats-reaction-rogers-el-sayed"]," from Democratic leaders and may have mobilized some Black voters to turn out for El-Sayed on Election Day."]},{"k":"p","s":[["“I felt like she pimped my community,”","https://x.com/ABC/status/2117648241458352569"]," one Black voter from Detroit told ABC News in response to Stevens’ last-minute endorsement of Rogers."]}],"chars":6364},"https://theconversation.com/the-uk-citizenship-test-is-elitist-it-needs-an-overhaul-296097":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-18T17:08Z","sha":"1d320b8cfcb230b6930280cc78212aa7dce90079cdd72578ae29e3cd9039112c","read":"https://theconversation.com/the-uk-citizenship-test-is-elitist-it-needs-an-overhaul-296097","bytes":180991,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"The UK citizenship test is elitist – it needs an overhaul","by":[{"n":"Anna Tuckett","r":"Senior Lecturer in Anthropology, Brunel University of London"}],"pub":"2026-11-18T15:25:11Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["The UK citizenship test – known as the Life in the UK test – was launched in 2005. Since its inception, the test has been mocked for its “pub quiz” style questions, which many people born and raised in the UK struggle to answer."]},{"k":"p","s":["For thousands of people, the test is what stands between them and a stable, settled life in the UK, as failing it can mean being denied indefinite leave to remain. And while the questions may seem trivial, they highlight a more serious debate about ",["British identity","https://theconversation.com/topics/british-identity-62682"]," and society."]},{"k":"p","s":["As the government sets out changes to the country’s ",["settlement and citizenship requirements","https://www.gov.uk/government/speeches/home-secretary-earned-settlement-statement"],", a ",["“refresh”","https://questions-statements.parliament.uk/written-questions/detail/2026-07-03/15780/"]," of the test has been announced."]},{"k":"p","s":["The test was first introduced in 2005, during a time of ",["heightened public concern","https://irr.org.uk/article/the-death-of-multiculturalism/"]," around citizenship, national identity, integration and ",["multiculturalism","https://theconversation.com/topics/multiculturalism-984"],". However, its current form reflects significant changes made under the Conservative-Liberal Democrats coalition government in 2013."]},{"k":"p","s":["These included replacing practical information about education, healthcare, policing and neighbourhood safety with historical and “cultural” knowledge. New topics included the Wars of the Roses, Jane Austen novels, the achievements of Sir Francis Drake and major sports events."]},{"k":"p","s":["The 2013 changes also removed the option to take a language and citizenship course instead of a multiple-choice test, in a bid to ",["toughen up settlement requirements","https://www.gov.uk/government/news/tougher-language-requirements-announced-for-british-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["While there are no state-funded classes to help candidates prepare for the test, there is an official Life in the UK Handbook. But just reading the handbook is often not enough to pass the test. Those with lower levels of formal education struggle to understand and absorb the handbook’s dense 180-page summary of British values, history, society and politics."]},{"k":"p","s":["Many therefore turn to privately run training centres which, for a fee, help candidates to prepare. I have conducted long-term ethnographic research in several of these centres across London."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attendees hailed from many countries, although often from former British colonies. Many had lived in the UK for years, and several had even been to school in the country."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["How the UK’s immigration system splits families apart – by design","https://theconversation.com/how-the-uks-immigration-system-splits-families-apart-by-design-261134"]]},{"k":"p","s":["The test’s more practical questions – such as “What is the name of the UK currency?” – were well known by applicants. But much of the handbook’s contents were unfamiliar to them despite many having lived in the country for a long time."]},{"k":"p","s":[["My research","https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/1070289X.2025.2593189"]," found a notable disconnect between the way the handbook and test represent Britishness and the applicants’ everyday experiences in the country."]},{"k":"h","s":["A Guide for New Residents"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Life in the UK test highlights many of the tensions and contradictions that surround the contemporary boundaries of Britishness. Even the handbook’s subtitle – A Guide for New Residents – is discordant. Many of those I met who were taking the test had lived in the UK for decades, and were already well integrated into their local communities."]},{"k":"p","s":["My respondents may not have been regulars at the local pub, but they all worked, paid taxes, watched popular TV shows, chatted with their neighbours and sent their children to local schools."]},{"k":"p","s":["Despite being already embedded in everyday British life, many of these people had failed the test, which features questions on roast beef, the Proms, the British monarchy and saints of the middle ages. Applicants had to answer questions such as:"]},{"k":"p","s":["What did St Augustine and St Columba do during the Anglo-Saxon Period?"]},{"k":"p","s":["A. They invented new farming techniques"]},{"k":"p","s":["B. They led an uprising in Wales"]},{"k":"p","s":["C. They helped to spread Christianity across Britain"]},{"k":"p","s":["D. They fought courageously against the Romans"]},{"k":"p","s":["Far from signalling a failure of integration, my research shows that these test failures were a product of the handbook’s ",["antiquated, cliched and elitist representation of “Britishness”","https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/1070289X.2025.2593189"],". The people I spoke to had failed the test because the Britain it presented, which also seemed to equate being British with being white."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Too often learning ‘British history’ means learning ‘English history’ – but overburdened schoolteachers are not to blame","https://theconversation.com/too-often-learning-british-history-means-learning-english-history-but-overburdened-schoolteachers-are-not-to-blame-214529"]]},{"k":"h","s":["A Long and Illustrious History"]},{"k":"p","s":["Perhaps the clearest way in which the UK citizenship test process actively associates Britishness with whiteness is through its account of British history. The handbook chapter titled A Long and Illustrious History focuses on monarchs and battles, and reads like an outdated history textbook."]},{"k":"p","s":["Reflecting the idea that British identity has ancient roots, the chapter traces British history from the stone age to Brexit and beyond. But this account of the country’s history is more remarkable for what it leaves out than for what it includes."]},{"k":"p","s":["A group of historians – which includes David Olusoga and Yasmin Khan – have ",["called for a review","https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2020/jul/22/home-office-urged-to-correct-false-slavery-information-in-citizenship-test"]," of the test. They argue that the handbook misrepresents slavery and empire by presenting the abolition of slavery as, in the historians’ words, a “British achievement” in which the enslaved “played no part”, while colonial protests, uprisings and independence movements are missing from the record."]},{"k":"p","s":["Discussions about the Life in the UK test tend to focus on its trivial content, widely seen as irrelevant to everyday life and unfamiliar even to those who have grown up in the country. But this emphasis on triviality detracts from what many see as the test’s racist and exclusionary message about what constitutes authentic Britishness. The test itself is therefore anything but trivial."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attempts to control who can be deemed truly British are nothing new. The version of British history and culture presented in the Life in the UK test is just one part of a ",["long history","https://blogs.lse.ac.uk/politicsandpolicy/commonwealth-hostile-environment/"]," of British nationality and citizenship policy, much of which reflects a desire to equate authentic Britishness with whiteness."]},{"k":"p","s":["This persistent version of authentic Britishness is not only discriminatory towards immigrants, but also towards many British people, in particular those for whom migration is part of their identity. The citizenship test was, in theory, introduced to produce social cohesion. In its current form it is an expression of a particular ideology of Britishness – one that fosters division and alienation."]}],"chars":6115}};
